`ROOMS`, `roomReverb`, `VOICE_LIMITS`; types `Audio`, `AudioOptions`, `AudioState`, `AudioInfo`, `PlayOptions`, `Sound`, `ListenerPose`, `GestureTarget`, `AudioBus`, `MixerInfo`, `MusicChange`, `MusicPosition`, `Quantize`, `RoomName`, `RoomSpec`, `VoiceLimits`.\n\n**Sound for places (WP 13.22)**: a room's reverb out of its size and what it is made of (Sabine's RT60), the walls between a sound and the listener counted, each muffling it more.\n`roomAcoustics`, `ABSORPTION`, `CONTENTS`, `wallsBetween`, `muffling`, `OCCLUSION`; types `RoomMake`.\n\n**The engine in a page (WP 2.7)**: createEngine reads the routes, starts the scene with its view, publishes window.__engine, warms up and runs the frame loop; createHeadless({ view: true }) builds the same view in Node.\n`createEngine`, `parseRoutes`, `routeQuery`; types `Engine`, `EngineOptions`, `Routes`, `CameraInfo`, `PlayResult`, `PlayIntoOptions`, `ViewChange`.\n\n**A page's own presentation (WP 9.5)**: createEngine's onFrame, once per drawn frame, with the run to read and the camera.\ntypes `EngineFrame`, `FrameWorld`, `CameraPose`.\n\n**Touch controls (WP 3.12; built, not tested, ADR-0021)**: a page's touch layout (the corner fan's buttons and the menu button) for createEngine's touchLayout and onMenu, the touch device on input.touch, and the touch codes it writes.\n`defineTouchLayout`, `getTouchLayout`, `touchCode`; types `TouchLayout`, `TouchLayoutSpec`, `TouchButtonSpec`, `TouchDevice`, `StickView`, `TouchSetting`.\n\n**Level meshes v2 and the cutaway (WP 4.4)**: galleries, stairs, the dais, pillars with plinths and capitals and brazier stands as recipe shapes; walls facing an outside camera cut low and pillars before the hero as stumps.\n`createCutaway`, `planCutaway`; types `Cutaway`, `CutawayReport`, `CutTarget`, `LevelCut`, `CutWhen`, `PartCut`.\n\n**Instancing and puppets (WP 3.8)**: batches of instanced copies in pages above r182's 1,000-slot uniform path; puppet bodies as data (one line per part on the humanoid skeleton's bones, mirrored parts, material slots), compiled per build and drawn as one rigid-skinned mesh per character or as instanced parts for crowds; blob shadows.\n`createInstancedBatch`, `defineBody`, `getBody`, `compileBody`, `recolor`, `createPuppet`, `createPuppetBatches`, `createBlobShadows`, `blobScale`; types `InstancedBatch`, `InstancedBatchOptions`, `InstancedBatchStats`, `InstanceColor`, `Body`, `BodySpec`, `BodyPart`, `BodyPoint`, `BodyLength`, `PartOptions`, `CompiledBody`, `BodyPiece`, `PieceShape`, `Puppet`, `PuppetMaterials`, `PuppetBatches`, `BlobShadows`.\n\n**The HTML/CSS overlay (WP 6.5)**: world-anchored labels and damage numbers placed from projected coordinates each frame (three.js's CSS2DRenderer pattern), HUD lines and a crosshair over the canvas; ui.state() for tests.\n`createOverlay`, `DAMAGE_NUMBERS`, `uiState`; types `Overlay`, `OverlayOptions`, `HudOptions`, `HudPlace`, `Label`, `LabelOptions`, `DamageOptions`, `WorldPoint`, `Anchor`, `OverlayCamera`, `UiState`, `UiElementState`.\n\n**The widgets (WP 10.6)**: bars, hearts and boxes, the dialog box and the menu as HTML/CSS over the overlay, reading the page's input (its system layer) and asking the page for sound cues; a gamepad's cursor over any panel. A menu sends the picks that change play as input (`send`), so replays hold them.\n`createBar`, `createHearts`, `createBox`, `createPadCursor`, `createDialog`, `createMenu`.\n\n**The store (WP 10.9)**: what a game keeps across sessions (high scores, progress, its settings) in the page's localStorage under the game's prefix, versioned and checked on load; memory in Node and in the isolated modes.\n`createStore`, `memoryBackend`.\n\n**Lights, shadows, atmosphere and sky (WP 7.1)**: light kinds for a level's light spots, a fixed pool of point lights near the focus with a shadow budget by quality tier, and sky presets (background, dome, backdrop, sun, ambient light, fog) that a sky puts on a scene.\n`defineLight`, `defineSky`, `createSky`; types `LightEntry`, `LightSource`, `SkyEntry`, `SkySpec`, `Sky`.\n\n**Materials v2 (WP 7.2)**: the same material data drawn in four styles (lambert, toon, flat, pbr), switched at run time with every style warmed; the toon look (bands and rim) as uniforms; outline shells for meshes and instanced batches.\n`createStyleSet`, `MATERIAL_STYLES`, `TOON_LOOK`, `createOutline`, `OUTLINE_MODES`; types `MaterialStyle`, `StyleSet`, `StyleSetOptions`, `ToonLook`, `ToonUniforms`, `Outline`, `OutlineMode`, `OutlineOptions`, `OutlineShells`.\n\n**Post-processing (WP 7.4, 13.32)**: one chain every frame draws through, every filter a uniform with an amount, scoped by part; looks as data (a material style, a filter chain, the sky, WP 7.8) that combine looks; objects tagged by part.\n`createPost`, `POST_SETTINGS`, `definePostSettings`, `setPart`, `PARTS`, `defineLook`, `FILTER_FIELDS`, `FILTER_NAMES`, `SCOPES`, `PALETTES`, `STYLIZE_KINDS`; types `Post`, `PostOptions`, `Part`, `PostTag`, `LookEntry`, `LookSpec`, `FilterName`, `Scope`, `FilterChain`, `FilterSpec`, `CombineLayer`, `PostShow`.\n\n**Props drawn (WP 4.5)**: every prop part a batch of the instancing service, posed by its body, the flames dancing on the visual streams, the light spots flickering, for the light pool; a part's geometry and where it stands (its matrix in the prop's frame), for a prop's tests.\n`createPropMeshes`, `FLICKER`, `buildPropPart`, `partMatrix`; types `PropMeshes`, `PropMeshesOptions`, `PropMeshPose`, `PropLight`.\n\n**Crowd rendering and pose LOD (WP 5.4)**: thousands of humanoids, blobs and floaters in a few dozen draw calls over the instancing service, each body seen through bands of detail by its distance (the animator's pose level, capes), culled by the view; the blob and floater bodies as data.\n`createCrowd`, `createCrowdLod`, `CROWD_LOD`, `BLOB_BODY`, `blobBody`, `FLOATER_BODY`, `QUADRUPED_BODY`; types `Crowd`, `CrowdDraw`, `CrowdRigDraw`, `CrowdStats`, `RigBody`, `RigPart`, `RigJoints`, `RigShape`, `CrowdLod`, `CrowdLodOptions`, `CrowdLodCounts`, `CrowdBand`, `CrowdBandSpec`, `BlobFeatures`.\n\n**Performance counters (WP 5.5)**: what `__engine.stats()` returns, means in ms and the renderer's counts, never fps.\ntypes `EngineStats`.\n\n**The texture library (v2, WP 7.3)**: a level's whole floor as a texture generator (define it under a game's id), with moss at the walls' feet, a rune circle on each dais and contact shadows along every block's foot.\n`levelFloorTexture`; types `LevelFloorOptions`, `ContactShadowOptions`, `FloorMossOptions`, `FloorRuneOptions`.\n\n**Clips in pages (WP 8.4)**: three.js's AnimationClip and AnimationMixer, for presentation only (a page plays a baked clip on a puppet with clipJSON and AnimationClip.parse); the sim samples the same tracks through the clip layer. The mannequin: the Quaternius figure the library was measured on, as a body and a build.\n`AnimationClip`, `AnimationMixer`, `defineMannequin`, `mannequinBody`, `MANNEQUIN_SLOTS`; types `MannequinData`.\n\n**Effects (WP 6.4)**: particles as data (emitters: shardfall's presets, the 2D engine's kinds, event effects), drawn with telegraphs on the floor, socket trails, bolts and camera shake by a view's effects; never part of the hash.\n`createEffects`, `FX_BUDGET`, `BOLT`, `defineEmitter`, `getEmitter`, `TRAIL_TINTS`, `ScreenShake`, `SHAKE`; types `Effects`, `EffectsOptions`, `FxEventPayload`, `FxStats`, `Emitter`, `EmitterSpec`, `EmitterLayer`, `ParticleFields`, `FxLight`, `BurstOptions`, `ParticleStats`, `TrailSampleLike`.\n\n**The feel kit (WP 13.4)**: courses, scripted runs of a scene and the numbers measured on them (`node x feel`); the runner and its verdicts; the owner's feel panel and copy as profile.\n`defineCourse`, `getCourse`, `listCourses`, `METRICS`, `runCourse`, `createFeelPanel`, `tunedSpec`, `profileText`; types `Course`, `Measure`, `Metric`, `CourseResult`, `CourseSample`, `MeasureResult`, `FeelPanel`, `FeelRow`, `FeelInspector`.\n\n**Camera modes (WP 2.5, WP 3.9, WP 13.8)**: a code to a camera, each mode's factory, and a game's own.\n`readCameraCode`, `createCamera`, `createShoulderCamera`, `SHOULDER`, `createFollowCamera`, `FOLLOW_RIG`, `createFirstCamera`, `createChaseCamera`, `createViewCamera`, `followCamera`, `defineCamera`, `makePose`, `poseForward`, `poseRight`, `poseUp`, `poseTarget`; types `AnyCamera`, `AnyCameraSpec`, `ShoulderInput`, `ShoulderSpec`, `FollowInput`, `FollowSpec`, `FollowCamera`, `FollowSteps`, `CameraKindSpec`, `Camera`, `CameraInput`.\n\n**The rig a view steps (WP 13.8)**: blends on live switches, the view effects, the view settings cam.*.\n`createCameraRig`, `rigOptions`, `CAMERA_SETTINGS`, `blendCameras`, `BLEND_TIME`, `createCameraEffects`, `applyEffects`, `cameraPlayer`, `apexFov`, `EFFECTS`; types `CameraRig`, `RigOptions`, `RigInput`, `CameraPlayer`, `EffectWeights`, `EffectsFrame`.\n<!-- api-map:end -->\n/**\n * @file The starter game's page (labs/game/index.html): it starts the engine (`createEngine`, engine/app/engine.ts) on\n * the scene `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) with the arena's text registered for the view, offers the bot's\n * replay to `?replay=bot`, and shows the round each drawn frame in the HTML/CSS overlay's HUD: the gems, the clock,\n * the controls, the best round kept across sessions (labs/game/best.ts, through the engine's store) and, when the\n * round ends, how it ended. Enter then starts a new round on the next seed. Escape (or the pad's Start) pauses the\n * round under a menu (`createMenu`: Resume, New round), which keeps its keys out of play while it is open\n * (`createEngine({ modal })`); the store keeps the best round and any keys rebound (`createEngine({ store })`). The\n * camera is the chase camera unless the URL names one (`?cam=iso`, `?cam3=orbit`).\n *\n * Everything else a page does (routes, the renderer, the frame loop, the devices, `window.__engine`, the error\n * overlay, the touch controls) is the engine's, so this file is the game's own presentation only. It reads the run\n * and never changes it: the HUD cannot change the hash.\n *\n * Game code: it imports only the engine's public API (engine/index.ts) and the game's own files.\n *\n * Open it at http://127.0.0.1:5173/labs/game/ (`npm run dev`): `?seed=7&game.gems=20` plays another round,\n * `?replay=bot` the bot's, `?cam=iso` another camera. Headless, `node x shot labs/game` reports what it draws.\n */\n/// <reference types=\"vite/client\" />\nimport { createEngine, createMenu, createStore, type Engine, type EngineFrame, type Menu } from '../../engine';\nimport { bestOf, recordBest } from './best';\nimport { ARENA_TEXT, play, type Round } from './scenes/play';\n\n/** The page's query, with the chase camera when it names none: it follows the player round the arena. */\nconst search = new URLSearchParams(location.search);\nif (!search.has('cam') && !search.has('cam3')) search.set('cam3', 'chase');\n\n/** The game's replays, by name (`?replay=bot`), as text loaded on demand. */\nconst replays = { bot: () => import('./replays/bot.replay.json?raw').then((module) => module.default) };\n\n/** The started engine; null until `createEngine` resolves (its first frames are drawn before that). */\nlet engine: Engine | null = null;\n\n/** Whether the round on screen has ended, so Enter starts the next. */\nlet ended = false;\n\n/** The game's store: its best round across sessions; a replay's page plays in its demo mode, so it sets none. */\nconst store = createStore({ prefix: 'my3dge-game:', mode: search.has('replay') ? 'demo' : 'play' });\n\n/** The fastest won round kept (s), and the run whose clock the page saw running, with the steps it started with. */\nlet best = bestOf(store);\nlet seen: { world: object; steps: number } | null = null;\n\n/** The pause menu while it is open; null while the round plays. */\nlet paused: Menu | null = null;\n\n/** Opens the pause menu over the paused round, or reads it a frame: Resume (or Escape again), New round. */\nfunction pauseMenu(dt: number): void {\n  const [inspector, ui, input] = [engine?.inspector, engine?.ui, engine?.input];\n  if (!inspector || !ui || !input) return;\n  const close = () => {\n    paused?.remove();\n    paused = null;\n    inspector.resume();\n  };\n  if (paused) return void paused.update(dt);\n  if (!input.pressed('pause')) return;\n  inspector.pause();\n  const items = [\n    { label: 'Resume', id: 'resume' },\n    { label: 'New round', id: 'new' },\n  ];\n  paused = createMenu(ui.root, items, { input, id: 'pause', title: 'Paused', onCancel: close, onPick: (_i, item) => {\n    if (typeof item === 'object' && item.id === 'new') inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\n    close();\n  } }); // prettier-ignore\n}\n\n/** Shows the round in the HUD: the gems, the clock, the controls, and how the round ended. */\nfunction showRound({ world }: EngineFrame): void {\n  const ui = engine?.ui;\n  const entity = world.query('round')[0] as unknown as { round: Round } | undefined;\n  if (!ui || !entity) return;\n  const { gems, collected, left, state } = entity.round;\n  if (seen?.world !== world) seen = state === 'playing' ? { world, steps: left + world.tick } : null;\n  const was = ended;\n  ui.hud('gems', `Gems ${collected} / ${gems}`, { at: 'top-left' });\n  ui.hud('clock', `${Math.ceil(left / world.hz)} s`, { at: 'top-right', color: left < 10 * world.hz ? '#ff8f6b' : '' });\n  ui.hud('keys', 'WASD: run · Space: jump · Shift: dash · Esc: pause', { at: 'bottom', keys: true });\n  ended = state !== 'playing';\n  if (ended && !was && state === 'won' && seen) best = recordBest(store, (seen.steps - left) / world.hz);\n  ui.hud('best', best === null ? null : `Best ${best.toFixed(1)} s`, { at: 'top-left' });\n  const end = state === 'won' ? 'Every gem! Enter: play again' : 'Time! Enter: play again';\n  ui.hud('end', ended ? end : null, { at: 'top' });\n}\n\nengine = await createEngine({\n  canvas: document.querySelector<HTMLCanvasElement>('#view')!,\n  scenes: [play.id],\n  levels: { 'level:arena': { text: ARENA_TEXT, file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts' } },\n  replays,\n  search: `?${search}`,\n  store,\n  modal: () => paused !== null,\n  onFrame: (frame) => {\n    pauseMenu(frame.dt);\n    showRound(frame);\n  },\n});\n\naddEventListener('keydown', (event) => {\n  const inspector = engine?.inspector;\n  if (event.code === 'Enter' && ended && inspector) inspector.seed(inspector.seed() + 1);\n});\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"utf-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, maximum-scale=1, user-scalable=no\" />\n    <meta name=\"theme-color\" content=\"#15171c\" />\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"../../engine/ui/touch.css\" />\n    <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:,\" />\n    <title>The starter game: my-3dge</title>\n    <!--\n      The starter game's page (labs/game/README.md): labs/game/main.ts starts the engine on the scene game:play and\n      shows the round in the HUD. Ready or error: until the engine publishes window.__engine, the inline script below\n      records a script that fails to load or throws, and shows it in #msg, so a broken page is one line of text,\n      never a blank one; `node x shot labs/game` reports the same headless.\n    -->\n    <style>\n      html,\n      body {\n        margin: 0;\n        height: 100%;\n        overflow: hidden;\n        background: #15171c;\n      }\n      canvas {\n        display: block;\n        width: 100vw;\n        height: 100vh;\n        height: 100dvh;\n        outline: none;\n        touch-action: none;\n      }\n      #msg {\n        position: fixed;\n        inset: 0;\n        display: flex;\n        align-items: center;\n        justify-content: center;\n        padding: 24px;\n        font:\n          18px system-ui,\n          sans-serif;\n        color: #c9ccd4;\n        text-align: center;\n        white-space: pre-line;\n        pointer-events: none;\n      }\n      #msg[hidden] {\n        display: none;\n      }\n    </style>\n    <script>\n      window.__engine = { ready: false, errors: [] };\n      function gameFailed(message) {\n        if (!window.__engine || typeof window.__engine.help === 'function') return; // the engine reports now\n        var fix = 'the console names the cause; node x shot labs/game reports it headless';\n        var record = { code: 'APP_START', message: 'the page failed to start: ' + message, fix: fix };\n        if (window.__engine.errors.length === 0) {\n          var msg = document.getElementById('msg');\n          if (msg) msg.textContent = record.code + ': ' + record.message + '\\nFix: ' + fix;\n        }\n        window.__engine.errors.push(record);\n      }\n      addEventListener('error', function (event) {\n        gameFailed(event.message || 'a script failed');\n      });\n      addEventListener('unhandledrejection', function (event) {\n        gameFailed(String((event.reason && event.reason.message) || event.reason));\n      });\n    </script>\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <canvas id=\"view\"></canvas>\n    <div id=\"msg\" role=\"status\" aria-live=\"polite\">Loading…</div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"./main.ts\" onerror=\"gameFailed('labs/game/main.ts did not load')\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n/**\n * @file The starter game's scene `game:play`: every new game begins as this one (tools/game/new-game.mjs copies\n * labs/game/ into it), so it is small, plays, and shows the parts a game is made of. The player, a humanoid on the\n * character controller, runs round the arena (`ARENA_TEXT` below: walls, two pillars, two low walls to jump) collecting\n * the gems the seed scatters, before the clock runs out. All the gems: won; the clock at 0: lost.\n *\n * The parts: a level as text, compiled for its physics bodies; settings (`game.*`, read when the scene starts, so they\n * change play and go in replays); components (`gem`, drawn as a small glowing box because it declares `x` and `z` in\n * metres; `round`, the score and the clock); the player (labs/game/cast/player.ts, an actor that reads the step's\n * intents: `move`, `jump`, `dash`); systems in the phase `rules`, after the actors' feet are read back; a named random\n * stream (`gems`); events (`gem`, `won`, `lost`) that pages, sounds and tests hear. The page is labs/game/main.ts, the\n * bot labs/game/bot.ts.\n *\n * The level's text lives here, not in a .txt file, since sim-side code reads no files; the page registers the same\n * text for the view (labs/game/main.ts).\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts, so `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts` runs it in Node.\n *\n * @example\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --steps 600\n * // node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --set game.gems=3 --seed 7\n * ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')?.position; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  addLevelBodies,\n  compileLevel,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineScene,\n  defineSettings,\n  physicsOf,\n  type ActorComponent,\n  type World,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\n\n/** The arena: 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls (0.75 m) to jump, the spawn `@`. */\nexport const ARENA_TEXT = `---\ndescription: The starter game's arena. 18 × 14 m inside walls 3 m high, two 2 × 2 m pillars, two low walls 0.75 m high that the player jumps, and the player's spawn.\n---\n##################\n#................#\n#..@.............#\n#.......PP.......#\n#.......PP.......#\n#................#\n#....w......w....#\n#....w......w....#\n#................#\n#.......PP.......#\n#.......PP.......#\n#................#\n#................#\n##################\n`;\n\n/** The arena, compiled: its colliders for physics, its tiles for the gems and the bot's paths. */\nexport const ARENA = compileLevel(ARENA_TEXT, { file: 'labs/game/scenes/play.ts', name: 'arena' });\n\n/** The game's settings: each is reachable through `x set`, URL parameters (`?game.gems=3`) and `__engine.set`. */\nexport const GAME_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\n  'game.gems': {\n    type: 'integer',\n    default: 10,\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 40,\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How many gems the seed scatters.',\n  },\n  'game.seconds': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 30,\n    minimum: 5,\n    maximum: 600,\n    unit: 's',\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How long the player has to collect them all.',\n  },\n  'game.speed': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 6,\n    minimum: 1,\n    maximum: 20,\n    unit: 'm/s',\n    when: 'scene',\n    description: 'How fast the player runs.',\n  },\n});\n\n/** A gem: where it floats and how it looks (the page draws a component that declares x and z in metres). */\nexport const GEM = defineComponent('gem', {\n  description: 'A gem to collect: where it floats, its spin and how it is drawn.',\n  fields: {\n    x: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'East.' },\n    y: { type: 'number', default: 0.5, unit: 'm', description: 'Up: the bottom of its box.' },\n    z: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'm', description: 'South.' },\n    yaw: { type: 'number', default: 0, unit: 'rad', description: 'Its spin.' },\n    size: { type: 'number', default: 0.4, unit: 'm', description: 'The side of its box.' },\n    material: { type: 'string', default: 'material:glow', description: 'What it is drawn with.' },\n  },\n});\n\n/** The round: the score, the clock and how it ended. One entity holds it. */\nexport const ROUND = defineComponent('round', {\n  description:\n    'The round: gems collected of the total, the steps left on the clock, and whether it is playing, won or lost.',\n  fields: {\n    gems: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many gems the round scattered.' },\n    collected: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'How many the player has collected.' },\n    left: { type: 'integer', default: 0, description: 'The sim steps left on the clock (60 a second).' },\n    state: { type: 'string', default: 'playing', description: \"'playing', 'won' or 'lost'.\" },\n  },\n});\n\n/** The round, as the component holds it. */\nexport type Round = { gems: number; collected: number; left: number; state: 'playing' | 'won' | 'lost' };\n\n/** The scene's components, typed. */\nexport type GameComponents = {\n  gem: { x: number; y: number; z: number; yaw: number; size: number; material: string };\n  round: Round;\n  actor: ActorComponent;\n};\n\n/** How close the player's feet come to a gem to collect it, m (on the ground plane). */\nexport const REACH = 0.8;\n\n/** How far from the spawn the gems keep, m, so the first one is never collected without moving. */\nconst CLEAR = 3;\n\n/** Where the player starts: the level's spawn `@`. */\nconst START = ARENA.spawns.find((spawn) => spawn.name === 'hero')!.position;\n\n/** The floor tiles a gem may float over: open floor (`.`), at least `CLEAR` metres from the spawn, in reading order. */\nfunction gemTiles(): number[] {\n  const tiles: number[] = [];\n  ARENA.tiles.forEach((char, i) => {\n    const x = ((i % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    const z = (Math.floor(i / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    if (char === '.' && Math.hypot(x - START[0], z - START[2]) >= CLEAR) tiles.push(i);\n  });\n  return tiles;\n}\n\n/** Scatters `count` gems over distinct floor tiles drawn from the stream `gems`: each seed lays them its own way. */\nfunction scatterGems(w: World<GameComponents>, count: number): void {\n  const tiles = gemTiles();\n  const rng = w.rng('gems');\n  for (let k = 0; k < count && tiles.length > 0; k++) {\n    const [tile] = tiles.splice(rng.int(0, tiles.length - 1), 1);\n    const x = ((tile % ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    const z = (Math.floor(tile / ARENA.cols) + 0.5) * ARENA.tile;\n    w.spawn({ gem: { x, z, yaw: rng.range(0, Math.PI) } });\n  }\n}\n\n/** Ends the round: the player stops reading intents (and so stands still), and the event says how it ended. */\nfunction endRound(w: World<GameComponents>, round: Round, state: 'won' | 'lost'): void {\n  round.state = state;\n  for (const e of w.query('actor')) {\n    e.actor.player = false;\n    e.actor.intents = {};\n  }\n  w.emit(state, { collected: round.collected, gems: round.gems, left: round.left });\n}\n\n/**\n * Spins the gems, collects those an actor's feet reach, and ends the round when the last one goes. A despawn waits for\n * the end of the step, so a gem taken this step is remembered: two actors never count it twice.\n */\nfunction collect(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  for (const gem of w.query('gem')) gem.gem.yaw += 2 * w.dt;\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  const taken = new Set<number>();\n  for (const { actor } of w.query('actor')) {\n    for (const gem of w.query('gem')) {\n      if (taken.has(gem.id) || Math.hypot(gem.gem.x - actor.x, gem.gem.z - actor.z) > REACH) continue;\n      taken.add(gem.id);\n      w.despawn(gem.id);\n      round.collected += 1;\n      w.emit('gem', { id: gem.id, x: gem.gem.x, z: gem.gem.z, collected: round.collected });\n    }\n  }\n  if (round.collected >= round.gems) endRound(w, round, 'won');\n}\n\n/** Runs the clock down a step at a time (game time is whole steps, never summed seconds); at 0 the round is lost. */\nfunction clock(w: World<GameComponents>): void {\n  const [{ round }] = w.query('round');\n  if (round.state !== 'playing') return;\n  round.left = Math.max(0, round.left - 1);\n  if (round.left === 0) endRound(w, round, 'lost');\n}\n\n/** The starter game: collect every gem before the clock runs out. */\nexport const play = defineScene<GameComponents>('game:play', {\n  description: 'The starter game: run round the arena collecting the gems before the clock runs out.',\n  level: 'level:arena',\n  physics: true,\n  setup(w) {\n    addLevelBodies(physicsOf(w), ARENA);\n    const gems = w.settings.get<number>('game.gems');\n    w.spawn({ round: { gems, left: Math.round(w.settings.get<number>('game.seconds') * w.hz) } });\n    scatterGems(w, gems);\n    spawnPlayer(w, [START[0], START[1], START[2]], w.settings.get<number>('game.speed'));\n    w.systems.add('game.collect', collect, { phase: 'rules' });\n    w.systems.add('game.clock', clock, { phase: 'rules' });\n  },\n});\n\nexport default play;\n/**\n * @file The starter game's player: the character the keys move (the character controller's numbers: how it runs,\n * jumps and dashes) and the body it is drawn as, and `spawnPlayer`, which stands it in a scene. A game keeps its\n * cast here, one character a file, as the box keeps its hero, walkers, slimes and wisps (labs/box/cast/); its scenes\n * spawn them. `node x sim labs/game/scenes/play.ts --feel` measures how the player handles: response, top speed, the\n * jump's height and air time, the dash's reach.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * playerCharacter(6).speed; // 6: m/s\n * playerCharacter(6).jumpSpeed; // 9: m/s at take-off, about 1.27 m up, over the arena's 0.75 m low walls\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.ts\n */\nimport { createCharacter, spawnActor, type Character, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\n\n/** The player's take-off speed, m/s: about 1.27 m up under the controller's gravity, over a 0.75 m low wall. */\nexport const JUMP_SPEED = 9;\n\n/** The body the player is drawn as: the humanoid in the chibi build, empty-handed. */\nexport const PLAYER_BODY = Object.freeze({ build: 'build:chibi', weapon: 'none' });\n\n/** The player's character at `speed` m/s; createCharacter's defaults for the rest (its dash among them). */\nexport function playerCharacter(speed: number): Character {\n  return createCharacter({ speed, jumpSpeed: JUMP_SPEED });\n}\n\n/** Stands the player in `w` (a scene with physics) at `at`, facing `yaw`: an actor the step's intents move. */\nexport function spawnPlayer<C extends object>(\n  w: World<C>,\n  at: readonly [number, number, number],\n  speed: number,\n  yaw = 0,\n): number {\n  const character = playerCharacter(speed);\n  return spawnActor(w, { at: [at[0], at[1], at[2]], character, player: true, yaw, anim: { ...PLAYER_BODY } });\n}\n/**\n * @file The starter game's bot: game code that plays `game:play` (labs/game/scenes/play.ts) through intents, the way\n * a player's keys do, so a test or an agent plays the game with nobody at the keys. Each step it reads what a player\n * would see (`viewOf`: the player's feet and the gems left) and answers with the step's intents (`botIntents`: run\n * down the arena's flow field to the nearest gem, round the pillars and the low walls).\n *\n * The bot never reaches into the sim: it reads the engine's inspector (`state`) and writes intents through `step`, so\n * what it plays is recorded like a person's play, and `input.record()` turns it into a replay\n * (labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json). A game keeps its bot as the game grows: the tests ask it to win\n * (labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts), which proves the game can be won, on every seed they try.\n *\n * Game code, page-side: it imports only engine/index.ts and the game's own modules.\n *\n * @example\n * // import { createHeadless } from '../../engine';\n * // const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed: 3 });\n * // const end = playBot(engine); // { state: 'won', steps: 1234 }\n * botIntents({ player: { x: 3.5, z: 2.5 }, gems: [{ x: 3.5, z: 9.5 }] }).move; // [0, 1]: south, toward the gem\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.test.ts\n */\nimport { NavGrid, type Headless, type Intents } from '../../engine';\nimport { ARENA, type Round } from './scenes/play';\n\n/** A point on the ground, m: x east, z south. */\nexport interface GroundSpot {\n  x: number;\n  z: number;\n}\n\n/** What the bot sees each step: the player's feet and the gems left. */\nexport interface BotView {\n  player: GroundSpot;\n  gems: readonly GroundSpot[];\n}\n\n/** The arena's walkable grid: the flow fields the bot follows go round its pillars and low walls. */\nconst GRID = new NavGrid(ARENA);\n\n/** How many headings the bot steers by: few, so its intents change seldom and its replays stay short. */\nexport const HEADINGS = 16;\n\n/** The intents for one step: run toward the nearest gem by walking distance; none when no gem is left. */\nexport function botIntents(view: BotView): Intents {\n  if (view.gems.length === 0) return {};\n  const goals = [...new Set(view.gems.map((gem) => GRID.nearestOpen(gem.x, gem.z)))].filter((tile) => tile >= 0);\n  const way = goals.length > 0 ? GRID.flowField(goals).direction(view.player.x, view.player.z) : null;\n  if (way) return { move: heading(way.x, way.z) };\n  // On a gem's tile (or nowhere the field leads): straight at the nearest gem.\n  const near = [...view.gems].sort((a, b) => distance(view.player, a) - distance(view.player, b))[0];\n  const d = distance(view.player, near);\n  return d < 1e-6 ? {} : { move: heading(near.x - view.player.x, near.z - view.player.z) };\n}\n\n/** The nearest of the `HEADINGS` directions to (x, z), as `move` takes it: two decimals cut toward 0, never past 1. */\nfunction heading(x: number, z: number): [number, number] {\n  const step = (2 * Math.PI) / HEADINGS;\n  const angle = Math.round(Math.atan2(x, z) / step) * step;\n  return [Math.trunc(Math.sin(angle) * 100) / 100 || 0, Math.trunc(Math.cos(angle) * 100) / 100 || 0];\n}\n\n/** The distance between two spots on the ground, m. */\nfunction distance(a: GroundSpot, b: GroundSpot): number {\n  return Math.hypot(b.x - a.x, b.z - a.z);\n}\n\n/** What the bot sees in a running engine: the player's feet and the gems left, read through the inspector. */\nexport function viewOf(engine: Headless): BotView {\n  const [player] = engine.state('actor').entities as unknown as { actor: GroundSpot }[];\n  const gems = (engine.state('gem').entities as unknown as { gem: GroundSpot }[]).map(({ gem }) => ({\n    x: gem.x,\n    z: gem.z,\n  }));\n  return { player: { x: player.actor.x, z: player.actor.z }, gems };\n}\n\n/** The round as it stands, read through the inspector. */\nexport function roundOf(engine: Headless): Round {\n  const [entity] = engine.state('round').entities as unknown as { round: Round }[];\n  return entity.round;\n}\n\n/** Plays the bot until the round ends or `limit` steps pass; returns how the round stands and the steps it took. */\nexport function playBot(engine: Headless, limit = 60 * 600): { state: Round['state']; steps: number } {\n  let steps = 0;\n  while (roundOf(engine).state === 'playing' && steps < limit) {\n    engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n    steps += 1;\n  }\n  return { state: roundOf(engine).state, steps };\n}\n/**\n * @file The starter game's tests (labs/game/scenes/play.ts): what every game made from it starts with, and keeps as it\n * grows. They run headless in Node (`npm test`), in a few seconds:\n * - its golden replay (labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json, the bot's play) gives its golden hashes, as `x replay`\n *   checks it: on another platform than the one that recorded them, two runs agree instead;\n * - a run continues exactly after a capture and a restore;\n * - the bot (labs/game/bot.ts) wins on 10 seeds, so the game can be won, however the gems fall;\n * - the clock runs out on a player who stands still, and the settings change play;\n * - two actors that reach a gem in the same step take it once.\n *\n * When the game's play changes on purpose, record the goldens again: `node x replay labs/game/replays/bot.replay.json\n * --browser sim --update` (in Node and Chromium), and say why in the commit.\n * @see labs/game/scenes/play.ts\n */\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { describe, expect, it } from 'vitest';\nimport { createHeadless } from '../../../engine';\nimport { defineScene, type World } from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { botIntents, playBot, roundOf, viewOf } from '../bot';\nimport { spawnPlayer } from '../cast/player';\nimport { play, type GameComponents } from './play';\n\n/** The golden replay: the bot's play from seed 1, with the goldens `x replay --update` recorded. */\nconst REPLAY = readFileSync(new URL('../replays/bot.replay.json', import.meta.url), 'utf8');\n\n/** This platform's golden key, as replays write it. */\nconst PLATFORM = `${process.platform}-${process.arch}`;\n\n/** Plays `text` from step 0 in a fresh engine and returns its hashes at the replay's checkpoints. */\nasync function replayed(text: string): Promise<Record<string, string>> {\n  const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play });\n  const result = await (engine.replay as (text: string) => Promise<{ hashes: Record<string, string> }>)(text);\n  return result.hashes;\n}\n\ndescribe('game:play', () => {\n  it('replays the bot’s play to its golden hashes', async () => {\n    const goldens = (JSON.parse(REPLAY) as { hashes: Record<string, Record<string, string>> }).hashes;\n    const first = await replayed(REPLAY);\n    if (goldens[PLATFORM]) expect(first).toEqual(goldens[PLATFORM]);\n    else expect(await replayed(REPLAY)).toEqual(first); // recorded elsewhere: the runs agree, as x replay judges it\n  });\n\n  it('continues exactly after a capture and a restore', async () => {\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed: 4 });\n    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n    const capture = engine.capture();\n    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n    const straight = engine.hash();\n    engine.restore(capture);\n    for (let k = 0; k < 120; k++) engine.step(1, botIntents(viewOf(engine)));\n    expect(engine.hash()).toBe(straight);\n  });\n\n  it('is won by the bot on 10 seeds', async () => {\n    for (let seed = 1; seed <= 10; seed++) {\n      const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, seed });\n      expect({ seed, ...playBot(engine) }).toMatchObject({ seed, state: 'won' });\n      expect(roundOf(engine).collected).toBe(roundOf(engine).gems);\n    }\n  });\n\n  it('is lost when the clock runs out, and its settings change play', async () => {\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: play, settings: { 'game.seconds': 5, 'game.gems': 3 } });\n    engine.step(5 * 60);\n    expect(roundOf(engine)).toMatchObject({ gems: 3, collected: 0, left: 0, state: 'lost' });\n    expect(viewOf(engine).gems).toHaveLength(3);\n  });\n\n  it('counts a gem once when two actors reach it in the same step', async () => {\n    const twin = defineScene<GameComponents>('game:twin', {\n      description: 'The starter, and two more players put on its gem in the first step: both reach it in the next.',\n      level: 'level:arena',\n      physics: true,\n      setup(w) {\n        play.setup(w);\n        const twins = (world: World<GameComponents>) => {\n          if ([...world.query('actor')].length > 1) return;\n          const [{ gem }] = world.query('gem');\n          for (const dx of [-0.3, 0.3]) spawnPlayer(world, [gem.x + dx, 0, gem.z], 6);\n        };\n        w.systems.add('test.twins', twins, { phase: 'rules' });\n      },\n    });\n    const engine = await createHeadless({ scene: twin, settings: { 'game.gems': 1 } }); // no neighbour within reach\n    engine.step(2);\n    expect([roundOf(engine).collected, roundOf(engine).state, engine.state('gem').entities.length]).toEqual([1, 'won', 0]); // prettier-ignore\n  });\n});\n# Engine feedback: weetare\n\nWhat this game needed from the my-3dge engine (at 2dbd829) and did not get. The owner collects this file\nfrom every game to improve the engine, so write each item for an engine agent who has never seen this repository:\nwhat you tried, what happened (the command, the error code), what you expected, and what you did instead.\n\n## Requests\n\n<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\n\n## Friction\n\n<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\n\n## Local engine patches\n\n<!--\n`npm run check` accepts an edited engine file only when it is listed here, one line each, its path in backticks:\n- `engine/path/to/file.ts`: why no workaround in the game would do, and what the engine should change instead.\n-->\nlabs/box/README.md\nlabs/box/clipFiles.ts\nlabs/box/index.html\nlabs/box/library.ts\nlabs/box/main.ts\nlabs/box/menu.ts\nlabs/box/menuControls.ts\nlabs/box/touch.ts\n\nlabs/box:\nREADME.md\ncast\nclipFiles.ts\nindex.html\nlevels\nlibrary.ts\nlooks\nmain.ts\nmenu.ts\nmenuControls.ts\nscenes\nsounds\ntouch.ts\n\nlabs/box/cast:\nhero.ts\nslime.ts\nwalker.ts\nwisp.ts\n\nlabs/box/levels:\nhall.txt\nroom.txt\n\nlabs/box/looks:\ndaylight.ts\nhall-floor.ts\ntorch-bloom.ts\ntorch-cel.ts\ntorch-fxaa.ts\ntorch-lit.ts\ntorch-pixel.ts\ntorch-toon.ts\n\nlabs/box/scenes:\nclips.ts\ncrowd-100.ts\ncrowd-1000.ts\ncrowd-5000.ts\nfight-1000.ts\nfight-foes.ts\nfight-hero.ts\nfight-rules.ts\nfight.ts\nhall-props.ts\nhall.ts\nragdoll.ts\nroom-hero.ts\nroom.ts\n\n","numLines":1221,"startLine":1,"totalLines":1221}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_012biEMd1vkMnmCWS2v61TfW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
