{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Np32owDYZw2tKqc19ArUGQ","type":"tool_result","content":"# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\n   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\n   (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n17587 .hubref/README.md\n/**\n * @file Clip mode, the animation library in the box (PLAN.md §10, WP 8.9; the Mocap Lab's clip mode,\n * `my-3d2dge:src/mocap.game.js`): the room (labs/box/levels/room.txt) as a physics level, the hero at its spawn and the\n * mannequin beside him, both playing a clip of the library through the clip layer in their animators (engine/sim\n * actorClips.ts), over the procedural rig. The mannequin is the figure the Quaternius clips were measured on\n * (`body:mannequin` on `build:mannequin`); the hero plays the clip retargeted to his build, and stays the player: he\n * walks under it (`box.clips.mask=upper` keeps his legs' own walk).\n *\n * Settings (`box.clips.*`, read every step, so a change plays at once and goes in replays): the clip, named\n * `<set>/<clip>` as `node x anim show` and `node x anim find` name it (a change crossfades to it from the pose on\n * screen); its rate; frame stepping (`box.clips.frame`, a frame of its bake at 30 a second, as `x anim bake` counts\n * them, held; -1 plays); the mirror and the mask. A one-shot holds its end 0.8 s, then plays again, as the Lab's did.\n * When the scene starts: who plays (`box.clips.cast`) and contact IK (`box.clips.ik`).\n *\n * The library's sets come from the registry (`defineClipSet`, the kind `clipset`): the box page registers every set\n * under data/anim/sets/ before it opens this scene (labs/box/main.ts), and so do tests/pages/replay.ts and the Node\n * hosts, `x sim`, `x replay` and tests (tools/anim/library.ts `defineLibrary`). Without them the setup fails with\n * `CORE_NO_ENTRY`, naming `defineClipSet`. Clips that travel play in place (their root motion is the layer's `root`,\n * which a game moves the body by). Its machine interface: `node x anim show <set>/<clip>` prints the clip this plays,\n * `__engine.describe('clipset')` and `node x describe clipset` list the sets, and the inspector shows each figure's\n * component `clips` (what plays, its time and weight) and its animator's layers (`__engine.anim(id)`).\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the box's own files.\n *\n * Tests: labs/box/scenes/clips.test.ts (every clip on the mannequin headless; `x anim show` and the setting select the\n * same clip, frame for frame; tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json's goldens), tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts (one clip\n * of each set in the page; `BOX_CLIPS=all` plays them all, a long run), tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts (the replay's\n * goldens while the page renders; live play replayed in Node).\n *\n * @example\n * // labs/box/?scene=clips&box.clips.clip=cmu/Cartwheel&cam=threequarter\n * // __engine.set('box.clips.clip', 'style100/Old_Walk'); __engine.set('box.clips.frame', 12)\n * // node x set box.clips.clip quaternius/Sword_Attack (in an x inspect session)\n * CLIPS_START; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]: the hero's spawn in the room; the mannequin stands 1.5 m east of him\n */\nimport {\n  addLevelBodies,\n  BAKE_FPS,\n  clipLayerOf,\n  clipSetIds,\n  createCharacter,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineScene,\n  defineSetBuild,\n  defineSettings,\n  getClipSet,\n  physicsOf,\n  playClip,\n  seekClip,\n  spawnActor,\n  type ClipPlay,\n  type World,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { HERO_BODY, heroCharacter } from '../cast/hero';\nimport { ROOM_HERO_LEVEL } from './room-hero';\nimport { boxSounds } from '../sounds/events';\n\n/** The scene's settings (see the file comment). */\nexport const CLIPS_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\n  'box.clips.clip': {\n    type: 'string',\n    default: 'quaternius/Dance_Loop',\n    description:\n      'The clip the figures play, <set>/<clip> as node x anim show names it (node x anim find lists them): a change crossfades to it.',\n  },\n  'box.clips.speed': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 1,\n    minimum: 0,\n    maximum: 2,\n    description: 'The rate it plays at: 1 as captured, 0.5 at half speed, 0 holds it.',\n  },\n  'box.clips.frame': {\n    type: 'integer',\n    default: -1,\n    minimum: -1,\n    maximum: 100_000,\n    description:\n      'Frame stepping: the frame of its bake held (from 0, 30 a second, as x anim bake counts them); -1 plays.',\n  },\n/**\n * @file The box's slime (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 5.7): a ball that hops after the hero, from Box 4 on. `SLIME` holds its\n * numbers, `CROWD_SLIME` its own component (`crowdSlime`: where it is in its hop and for how long, beside the crowd\n * agent the scene keeps), `makeSlime` draws one, and `steerSlime` moves it each step: on the floor it brakes, rests,\n * crouches and leaps; in the air it flies on until it lands.\n *\n * Its hop, the prototype's: after a rest it crouches for `SLIME.crouch`, then leaps (`hop`, engine/world/steer.ts)\n * `SLIME.reach` metres along the flow field toward the hero's tile, up at `SLIME.up` m/s, so it lands where it aimed\n * under its own gravity, onto a stair as well as across the floor; level with the hero it keeps to a ring round him\n * instead, leaping in from beyond it by what it lacks and out from inside it. A hop too short to bother with, or one\n * out of reach, waits a moment. After landing it rests for `SLIME.rest` plus up to `SLIME.restSpread`, drawn from the\n * crowd's stream.\n *\n * Its pounce (Box 5, WP 6.7): `SLIME_ATTACK`. Resting on its ring round the hero, cooled down and granted one of his\n * attack tokens, it squats for `wind` s, its line telegraph (`telegraph:boxPounce`) filling toward him, then leaps at\n * where he stood, up at `up` m/s, to land just short of him; touching him on the way takes `damage` hit points and\n * throws it back off him. Landed, it gives the token back and rests `rest` s plus up to `SLIME.restSpread`. A hit on\n * it breaks its pounce off. It has `health` hit points.\n *\n * Its numbers are the stress test's slime (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:200-203, 387-414`), in SI units\n * (PLAN.md Appendix C: 16 units a metre), as starting values (§9.0: similar, not identical): a ball of radius 6 units\n * → 0.375 m; leaps of 150 units/s up → 9.375 m/s (`HOP.up`), at most 44 units → 2.75 m (`HOP.reach`), after a crouch\n * of 0.28 s; a rest of 0.45 s plus up to 0.6 s; braking at 400 units/s² → 25 m/s²; its ring 34 units → 2.125 m, its\n * band 8 units → 0.5 m. Its first rest is drawn from its spawn, up to 1 s.\n *\n * Its body is drawn as a blob (a crowd body, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) in one of `SLIME.looks`, squashed by where it\n * is in its hop (`SLIME.squash`); the blob's spring makes the bounce.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * SLIME.reach; // 2.75: m, its longest hop\n * // steerSlime(physics, agent, slime, chase); // in the phase ai, each step\n * @see labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  HOP,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineTelegraph,\n  followFlow,\n  hop,\n  knockback,\n  launch,\n  setVelocity,\n  Vector3,\n  type CrowdAgent,\n  type Physics,\n  type Rng,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { levelWith, type Chase } from './walker';\n\n/** The prototype's units per metre (PLAN.md Appendix C). */\nconst UNITS = 16;\n\n/** The slime's numbers (see the file comment). */\nexport const SLIME = Object.freeze({\n  /** Its body: a ball (m). */\n  agent: Object.freeze({ shape: 'ball', radius: 6 / UNITS } as const),\n  /** How fast it leaps up (m/s), and its longest leap (m). */\n  up: HOP.up,\nx describe: ok: sky \"sky:noon\": 7 of 8 fields differ from the default\n* description = \"Noon by the clock: a clear sky dome, the sun high in the south, the lamps lit by their switches.\"\n* background = \"#9cc4ec\"\n  pointLights = 1\n* dome = {\"show\":true,\"turbidity\":2,\"rayleigh\":1,\"mieCoefficient\":0.005,\"mieDirectionalG\":0.8,\"exposure\":0.5}\n* sun = {\"color\":\"#fff0d8\",\"intensity\":2.6,\"azimuth\":0,\"elevation\":0.9}\n* ambient = {\"sky\":\"#c8d4ff\",\"ground\":\"#4a3f30\",\"intensity\":1.6}\n* fog = {\"color\":\"#c8daf0\",\"start\":40,\"end\":220,\"amount\":0.5,\"floor\":0,\"ceiling\":1.5,\"height\":0}\n* backdrop = {\"haze\":\"#c8e4f8\",\"tint\":\"#ffffff\",\"layers\":[{\"kind\":\"mountains\",\"color\":\"#7a98c8\",\"height\":0.95,...\n(a line above is cut short: the whole text is in out/describe/sky-sky-noon/describe.json)\nreport: out/describe/sky-sky-noon/report.json\nengine/ui/menu.ts:89:export function createMenu(parent: HTMLElement, items: readonly MenuItem[], options: MenuOptions): Menu {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-90-  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-91-  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-92-  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-93-  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\nengine/ui/menu.ts-94-  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\nengine/ui/menu.ts-95-  parent.append(el);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-96-  const repeat = createRepeat();\nengine/ui/menu.ts-97-  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\nengine/ui/menu.ts-98-  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\nengine/ui/menu.ts-99-  let index = 0;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-100-\nengine/ui/menu.ts-101-  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\nengine/ui/menu.ts-102-  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-103-    let at = from;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-104-    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-105-    return at;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-106-  };\nengine/ui/menu.ts-107-  const draw = () => {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-108-    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-109-    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-110-      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\nengine/ui/menu.ts-111-      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-112-    });\nengine/ui/menu.ts-113-  };\nengine/ui/menu.ts-114-  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-115-    if (!list.length) return;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-116-    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-117-    if (next === index) return;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-118-    index = next;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-119-    sound('move');","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d46f5b4-97b7-46a5-8fb8-5eac466a6eae","uuid":"02fabf0c-d05c-4625-95b1-0672b43a85bf","timestamp":"2026-11-05T09:44:27.933Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# AI Hub Session Protocol v1\n\nAn **AI Hub session** is up to four players, each on their own device,\nplaying rounds of games one after another. The hub runs everything around a\nround: the invite, the lobby, the seats and names, the network, the clock, the\nscoreboard and the results. This page defines how a game takes part in a\nround, and how the copies of a game send data to each other.\n\n**https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md**\n\nThe hub tests every game when it joins the library, with the same test\ndescribed in *Test it*, and keeps a game that fails it out of sessions.\n\n- Client: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/session.js\n- Harness: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/harness.html\n\nTo ask an agent for it, add this to the game's prompt:\n\n> This game must support AI Hub sessions. Follow\n> https://raw.githubusercontent.com/michaelcrosato/ai-hub/main/lib/hub/README.md\n> (AI Hub Session Protocol v1) and pass the harness's automatic check.\n\n---\n\n## Modes\n\nA game declares one mode.\n\n| Mode | What each copy runs | What the copies send each other |\n|---|---|---|\n| `parallel` | its own copy of the round | nothing |\n| `ghost` | its own copy of the round | each copy's own player: where it is and what it is doing |\n| `shared-world` | one world for all players, run by the host's copy | what each player does, to the host; the world, from the host |\n\n- **Parallel**: every player plays their own copy of the round, from the same\n  start. Each copy reports its score to the hub.\n- **Ghost**: as parallel, and each copy also shows the other players'\n  characters where they are, when they are in the same area of the game.\n  Those characters do not affect anything in the copy that shows them.\n- **Shared world**: all players play in one world. The host's copy runs that\n  world; the other copies send it what their own player does, and show the\n  world the host sends them.\n\nGames tagged with the older modes keep working: `race` is played as ghost,\n`co-op` and `versus` as shared world.\n\n---\n\n## A round\n\n1. The hub loads the game on every player's device, and the players get 10\n   to 30 seconds with the game's card: what the game is, how to win, the\n   controls. The card is the hub's, from the game's tags, or the game's own\n   (*The card*).\n2. The game connects and calls `ready()`.\n3. The round starts on the hub's clock, on every device at once.\n4. The game reports how it goes.\n5. The round ends when every player has a result, when the host of a shared\n   world finishes it, or when the hub calls time. The hub shows the results\n   over the game, then removes it.\n\n17587 .hubref/README.md\n/**\n * @file Clip mode, the animation library in the box (PLAN.md §10, WP 8.9; the Mocap Lab's clip mode,\n * `my-3d2dge:src/mocap.game.js`): the room (labs/box/levels/room.txt) as a physics level, the hero at its spawn and the\n * mannequin beside him, both playing a clip of the library through the clip layer in their animators (engine/sim\n * actorClips.ts), over the procedural rig. The mannequin is the figure the Quaternius clips were measured on\n * (`body:mannequin` on `build:mannequin`); the hero plays the clip retargeted to his build, and stays the player: he\n * walks under it (`box.clips.mask=upper` keeps his legs' own walk).\n *\n * Settings (`box.clips.*`, read every step, so a change plays at once and goes in replays): the clip, named\n * `<set>/<clip>` as `node x anim show` and `node x anim find` name it (a change crossfades to it from the pose on\n * screen); its rate; frame stepping (`box.clips.frame`, a frame of its bake at 30 a second, as `x anim bake` counts\n * them, held; -1 plays); the mirror and the mask. A one-shot holds its end 0.8 s, then plays again, as the Lab's did.\n * When the scene starts: who plays (`box.clips.cast`) and contact IK (`box.clips.ik`).\n *\n * The library's sets come from the registry (`defineClipSet`, the kind `clipset`): the box page registers every set\n * under data/anim/sets/ before it opens this scene (labs/box/main.ts), and so do tests/pages/replay.ts and the Node\n * hosts, `x sim`, `x replay` and tests (tools/anim/library.ts `defineLibrary`). Without them the setup fails with\n * `CORE_NO_ENTRY`, naming `defineClipSet`. Clips that travel play in place (their root motion is the layer's `root`,\n * which a game moves the body by). Its machine interface: `node x anim show <set>/<clip>` prints the clip this plays,\n * `__engine.describe('clipset')` and `node x describe clipset` list the sets, and the inspector shows each figure's\n * component `clips` (what plays, its time and weight) and its animator's layers (`__engine.anim(id)`).\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts and the box's own files.\n *\n * Tests: labs/box/scenes/clips.test.ts (every clip on the mannequin headless; `x anim show` and the setting select the\n * same clip, frame for frame; tests/replays/box-8-clips.replay.json's goldens), tests/e2e/box-clips.spec.ts (one clip\n * of each set in the page; `BOX_CLIPS=all` plays them all, a long run), tests/e2e/parity.spec.ts (the replay's\n * goldens while the page renders; live play replayed in Node).\n *\n * @example\n * // labs/box/?scene=clips&box.clips.clip=cmu/Cartwheel&cam=threequarter\n * // __engine.set('box.clips.clip', 'style100/Old_Walk'); __engine.set('box.clips.frame', 12)\n * // node x set box.clips.clip quaternius/Sword_Attack (in an x inspect session)\n * CLIPS_START; // [3.5, 0, 2.5]: the hero's spawn in the room; the mannequin stands 1.5 m east of him\n */\nimport {\n  addLevelBodies,\n  BAKE_FPS,\n  clipLayerOf,\n  clipSetIds,\n  createCharacter,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineScene,\n  defineSetBuild,\n  defineSettings,\n  getClipSet,\n  physicsOf,\n  playClip,\n  seekClip,\n  spawnActor,\n  type ClipPlay,\n  type World,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { HERO_BODY, heroCharacter } from '../cast/hero';\nimport { ROOM_HERO_LEVEL } from './room-hero';\nimport { boxSounds } from '../sounds/events';\n\n/** The scene's settings (see the file comment). */\nexport const CLIPS_SETTINGS = defineSettings({\n  'box.clips.clip': {\n    type: 'string',\n    default: 'quaternius/Dance_Loop',\n    description:\n      'The clip the figures play, <set>/<clip> as node x anim show names it (node x anim find lists them): a change crossfades to it.',\n  },\n  'box.clips.speed': {\n    type: 'number',\n    default: 1,\n    minimum: 0,\n    maximum: 2,\n    description: 'The rate it plays at: 1 as captured, 0.5 at half speed, 0 holds it.',\n  },\n  'box.clips.frame': {\n    type: 'integer',\n    default: -1,\n    minimum: -1,\n    maximum: 100_000,\n    description:\n      'Frame stepping: the frame of its bake held (from 0, 30 a second, as x anim bake counts them); -1 plays.',\n  },\n/**\n * @file The box's slime (PLAN.md §9.0, WP 5.7): a ball that hops after the hero, from Box 4 on. `SLIME` holds its\n * numbers, `CROWD_SLIME` its own component (`crowdSlime`: where it is in its hop and for how long, beside the crowd\n * agent the scene keeps), `makeSlime` draws one, and `steerSlime` moves it each step: on the floor it brakes, rests,\n * crouches and leaps; in the air it flies on until it lands.\n *\n * Its hop, the prototype's: after a rest it crouches for `SLIME.crouch`, then leaps (`hop`, engine/world/steer.ts)\n * `SLIME.reach` metres along the flow field toward the hero's tile, up at `SLIME.up` m/s, so it lands where it aimed\n * under its own gravity, onto a stair as well as across the floor; level with the hero it keeps to a ring round him\n * instead, leaping in from beyond it by what it lacks and out from inside it. A hop too short to bother with, or one\n * out of reach, waits a moment. After landing it rests for `SLIME.rest` plus up to `SLIME.restSpread`, drawn from the\n * crowd's stream.\n *\n * Its pounce (Box 5, WP 6.7): `SLIME_ATTACK`. Resting on its ring round the hero, cooled down and granted one of his\n * attack tokens, it squats for `wind` s, its line telegraph (`telegraph:boxPounce`) filling toward him, then leaps at\n * where he stood, up at `up` m/s, to land just short of him; touching him on the way takes `damage` hit points and\n * throws it back off him. Landed, it gives the token back and rests `rest` s plus up to `SLIME.restSpread`. A hit on\n * it breaks its pounce off. It has `health` hit points.\n *\n * Its numbers are the stress test's slime (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/20-sim.js:200-203, 387-414`), in SI units\n * (PLAN.md Appendix C: 16 units a metre), as starting values (§9.0: similar, not identical): a ball of radius 6 units\n * → 0.375 m; leaps of 150 units/s up → 9.375 m/s (`HOP.up`), at most 44 units → 2.75 m (`HOP.reach`), after a crouch\n * of 0.28 s; a rest of 0.45 s plus up to 0.6 s; braking at 400 units/s² → 25 m/s²; its ring 34 units → 2.125 m, its\n * band 8 units → 0.5 m. Its first rest is drawn from its spawn, up to 1 s.\n *\n * Its body is drawn as a blob (a crowd body, engine/sim/crowdBodies.ts) in one of `SLIME.looks`, squashed by where it\n * is in its hop (`SLIME.squash`); the blob's spring makes the bounce.\n *\n * Game code, sim-side: it imports only engine/sim-api.ts.\n *\n * @example\n * SLIME.reach; // 2.75: m, its longest hop\n * // steerSlime(physics, agent, slime, chase); // in the phase ai, each step\n * @see labs/box/cast/crowd.test.ts\n */\nimport {\n  HOP,\n  defineComponent,\n  defineTelegraph,\n  followFlow,\n  hop,\n  knockback,\n  launch,\n  setVelocity,\n  Vector3,\n  type CrowdAgent,\n  type Physics,\n  type Rng,\n} from '../../../engine/sim-api';\nimport { levelWith, type Chase } from './walker';\n\n/** The prototype's units per metre (PLAN.md Appendix C). */\nconst UNITS = 16;\n\n/** The slime's numbers (see the file comment). */\nexport const SLIME = Object.freeze({\n  /** Its body: a ball (m). */\n  agent: Object.freeze({ shape: 'ball', radius: 6 / UNITS } as const),\n  /** How fast it leaps up (m/s), and its longest leap (m). */\n  up: HOP.up,\nx describe: ok: sky \"sky:noon\": 7 of 8 fields differ from the default\n* description = \"Noon by the clock: a clear sky dome, the sun high in the south, the lamps lit by their switches.\"\n* background = \"#9cc4ec\"\n  pointLights = 1\n* dome = {\"show\":true,\"turbidity\":2,\"rayleigh\":1,\"mieCoefficient\":0.005,\"mieDirectionalG\":0.8,\"exposure\":0.5}\n* sun = {\"color\":\"#fff0d8\",\"intensity\":2.6,\"azimuth\":0,\"elevation\":0.9}\n* ambient = {\"sky\":\"#c8d4ff\",\"ground\":\"#4a3f30\",\"intensity\":1.6}\n* fog = {\"color\":\"#c8daf0\",\"start\":40,\"end\":220,\"amount\":0.5,\"floor\":0,\"ceiling\":1.5,\"height\":0}\n* backdrop = {\"haze\":\"#c8e4f8\",\"tint\":\"#ffffff\",\"layers\":[{\"kind\":\"mountains\",\"color\":\"#7a98c8\",\"height\":0.95,...\n(a line above is cut short: the whole text is in out/describe/sky-sky-noon/describe.json)\nreport: out/describe/sky-sky-noon/report.json\nengine/ui/menu.ts:89:export function createMenu(parent: HTMLElement, items: readonly MenuItem[], options: MenuOptions): Menu {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-90-  widgetStyle(parent.ownerDocument);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-91-  const { input, sound = () => {} } = options;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-92-  const el = uiElement(parent, 'ui-panel ui-menu', 'menu', options.id);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-93-  el.dataset.place = options.place ?? 'center';\nengine/ui/menu.ts-94-  if (options.title) el.append(Object.assign(uiElement(el, 'ui-menu-title', 'menu-title'), { textContent: options.title })); // prettier-ignore\nengine/ui/menu.ts-95-  parent.append(el);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-96-  const repeat = createRepeat();\nengine/ui/menu.ts-97-  let list: MenuItem[] = [];\nengine/ui/menu.ts-98-  let rows: HTMLElement[] = [];\nengine/ui/menu.ts-99-  let index = 0;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-100-\nengine/ui/menu.ts-101-  /** `index` stepped by `dir` until an enabled item (or all the way round). */\nengine/ui/menu.ts-102-  const skip = (from: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-103-    let at = from;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-104-    for (let k = 0; k < list.length && off(list[at]); k++) at = (at + dir + list.length) % list.length;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-105-    return at;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-106-  };\nengine/ui/menu.ts-107-  const draw = () => {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-108-    if (el.dataset.value !== String(index)) el.dataset.value = String(index);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-109-    rows.forEach((row, i) => {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-110-      const value = off(list[i]) ? 'disabled' : i === index ? 'selected' : '';\nengine/ui/menu.ts-111-      if (row.dataset.value !== value) row.dataset.value = value;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-112-    });\nengine/ui/menu.ts-113-  };\nengine/ui/menu.ts-114-  const move = (to: number, dir: 1 | -1) => {\nengine/ui/menu.ts-115-    if (!list.length) return;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-116-    const next = skip(((to % list.length) + list.length) % list.length, dir);\nengine/ui/menu.ts-117-    if (next === index) return;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-118-    index = next;\nengine/ui/menu.ts-119-    sound('move');","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Np32owDYZw2tKqc19ArUGQ","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
