r && x < x1 + clear && z > z0 - clear && z < z1 + clear); // prettier-ignore\n319:    description: 'Terrain: outdoor ground as a seeded heightfield (noise, hills, terraces, flattened footprints).',\n321:    defineWith: \"defineTerrain('<id>', { size, cell, origin, seed, height, hills, flats, … })\",\nx describe: ok: terrain: 16 fields, 0 entries\nTerrain: outdoor ground as a seeded heightfield (noise, hills, terraces, flattened footprints).\nids: none yet\n  size: array, m, required: Its extent along x and along z, each a whole number of cells: [24, 96].\n  cell: number, = 1, 0.25..8, m: The grid’s spacing: a height stands at every cell’s corners.\n  origin: array, = [0,0,0], m: Its north-west corner, at the height everything else is added to: [x, y, z].\n  seed: integer, = 0: The noise’s seed.\n  height: number, = 0, 0..inf, m: The noise’s range: rolling ground about this high (0: none).\n  scale: number, = 40, 1..inf, m: The size of the noise’s features.\n  octaves: integer, = 5, 1..8: The noise’s octaves.\n  ridges: number, = 0.5, 0..1: How much ridged noise is added: shardfall’s half.\n  hills: array, = []: Smooth domes added: { at: [x, z], radius, height } (m; a negative height digs a hollow).\n  terrace: number, = 0, 0..inf, m: Rounds heights to steps this high (0: smooth).\n  flats: array, = []: Footprints flattened: { rect: [x0, z0, x1, z1], height, margin } (m), the ground blending back over margin round each.\n  surface: string, = \"grass\": The surface tag underfoot (footsteps, particles).\n  steep: number, = 0.7, 0..inf, m/m: Ground rising this much a metre or more is steep (0.7: 35°).\n  steepSurface: string, = \"rock\": The surface tag on steep ground.\n  high: number, = 0, 0..inf, m: The high layer shows from this height over the origin up (0: none).\n… 2 more in out/describe/terrain/output.txt\nreport: out/describe/terrain/report.json\nx describe: ok: geometry: 4 fields, 7 entries\nShapes props, levels and bodies name by id: a builder of a three.js BufferGeometry with its parameters and a vertex budget.\nfallback: geometry:box\nids: geometry:box, geometry:frustum, geometry:limb, geometry:pillar, geometry:ramp, geometry:ring, geometry:roundedBox\n  description: string, required: What it is, in plain sentences.\n  params: object, = {}: Its parameters as schema fields (engine/core/schema.ts: type, default, description, minimum…), each with a defaul...\n  budget: integer, = 4096, 1..inf: The most vertices it may have at its default parameters (the geo QA family checks it).\n  create: function, required: The builder: (params) => BufferGeometry, standing on the ground, in metres, with normals and UVs in metres ...\n(a line above is cut short: the whole text is in out/describe/geometry/describe.json)\nreport: out/describe/geometry/report.json\nx describe: ok: material: 18 fields, 29 entries\nMaterials as data with three.js's classic parameters (color, map, roughness, emissive, flags); the engine decides how to draw them.\nfallback: material:default\nids: material:asphalt, material:barrel, material:barrelLid, material:barrelStaves, material:blobShadow, material:brick, material:carpet, material:checker, material:cloth, material:concrete, material:crate, material:default, material:flagstone, material:flame, material:glass, material:glow, material:hallFloor, material:iron, material:paint, … (10 more; all 29 in out/describe/material/describe.json)\n  description: string, = \"\": What it is for, in plain sentences.\n  color: string, = \"#ffffff\": The base colour, hex; it multiplies the map (three.js's color).\n  map: any, = null: The texture generator that fills the maps: a texture id ('texture:brick'), or { texture, seed, params, size, look, re...\n  roughness: number, = 1, 0..1: Microfacet roughness, 0 (mirror) to 1 (matte), for the styles that shade with it (pbr, WP 7.2).\n  metalness: number, = 0, 0..1: How metallic, 0 to 1, for the styles that shade with it (pbr, WP 7.2).\n  emissive: string, = \"#000000\": The colour