{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LGbvAeoxHaUDrCB2Roii1a","type":"tool_result","content":"2: * @file The atmosphere (PLAN.md WP 7.1): the fog and the ambient light a sky preset gives (engine/gfx/sky.ts).\n4: * Fog is range fog plus height fog, one TSL fog node on `scene.fogNode` whose numbers are all uniforms, so changing\n5: * them, or turning the fog off (`amount` 0), never rebuilds a shader. Range fog starts `start` metres past the focus\n7: * camera stands far back): `follow(camera, focus)` moves it each frame. Height fog lies on the floor: `height` at\n8: * `floor` (m), thinning to none at `ceiling`, and grows from nothing at the focus to whole at the range fog's end, so\n9: * the play area stays clear. The two combine as `1 − (1 − range)(1 − height)`, scaled by `amount`; `fogAt` is the same\n10: * sum on the CPU, for tests and tools. Materials with `fog: false` (the sky dome, the backdrop) are never fogged.\n14: * `register(warmup)` adds the fog to the warm-up's shader key (engine/gfx/warmup.ts reads `scene.fog`, never a fog\n17: * Invariants: presentation only, never in the hash; one fog node and one ambient light per atmosphere, made once; the\n18: * fog's numbers are render-group uniforms, so every object sees each frame's (engine/gfx/sky.ts says why).\n20: * Carried from `my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/50-frame.js:54-56` (the fog that starts a little past the hero, however\n25: * fogAt(spec, 30, 5, 30); // 0: the focus itself is clear\n26: * fogAt(spec, 100, 5, 30); // 1: 70 m past the focus\n33:import { float, fog, positionView, positionWorld, renderGroup, smoothstep, uniform } from 'three/tsl';\nTerminated                 WT_SEEDS=1 WT_ONLY=line timeout 100 npx vitest run labs/game/scenes/balance.test.ts -t \"meets\" 2>&1 | grep -E \"Error:\" | cut -c1-200 | head -4\n{\"table\":{\"reps\":{\"perfect\":973,\"human\":784,\"sloppy\":802,\"idle\":189}},\"problems\":[]}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"sessio