{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HVymL4xd5mdWqgeYLxoXsR","type":"tool_result","content":" * outline.ts's inverted hulls, wired to the stage (engine/gfx/stage.ts) round its props and its bodies. Every batch\n * of the props (engine/gfx/props.ts, a shell per page sharing its instance matrices, pushed away from each part's\n * centre) and every actor's puppet (a skinned shell bound to its skeleton, pushed along its normals, so the line\n * follows the posed body, first person's hidden pieces hidden in it too) gets its shell as it first appears, at\n * `sync()`, which the stage runs at the end of each draw, so the instances and the pieces match the frame's.\n *\n * A look asks for them (`shells: { width, color }`, engine/gfx/post/looks.ts), which the page's look hands over each\n * frame (engine/app/look.ts): `width` in pixels at 270 lines, scaled in the shader to the picture's lines in whole\n * pixels, so the line keeps its weight in every resolution mode; 0 hides every shell. Showing, hiding, the width and\n * the colour are visibility and uniforms: the shells are registered with the warm-up whatever the look, so switching\n * builds nothing. The ID pass leaves them out (`userData.outline`, engine/gfx/idpass.ts): the shells are the look's,\n * not objects of their own, and a shot's objects are the same in every look.\n2: * @file The stage's outline shells (PLAN.md WP 13.24; docs/PLAYGROUND.md §5.2's cel look): engine/gfx/materials/\n9: * A look asks for them (`shells: { width, color }`, engine/gfx/post/looks.ts), which the page's look hands over each\n10: * frame (engine/app/look.ts): `width` in pixels at 270 lines, scaled in the shader to the picture's lines in whole\n11: * pixels, so the line keeps its weight in every resolution mode; 0 hides every shell. Showing, hiding, the width and\n12: * the colour are visibility and uniforms: the shells are registered with the warm-up whatever the look, so switching\n13: * builds nothing. The ID pass leaves them out (`userData.outline`, engine/gfx/idpass.ts): the shells are the look's,\n23: * // const shells = createStageShells({ props: stage.props, actors: stage.actors });\n24: * // shells.set({ width: 1, color: '#141018' }); // the cel look's\n25: * // stage.draw(alpha); shells.sync();\n30:import { shellsOn, type FeatureReport } from './features';\n38:/** The lines a look's shell width is given at: scaled to the picture's height in whole pixels. */\n41:/** What a look asks of the shells: their width in pixels at 270 lines (0 for none), and their colour, hex. */\n43:  width: number;\n47:/** The stage's shells (see the file comment). */\nengine/gfx/materials/toon.ts:7: * sun's light; a rim, gated by each light (a fresnel step at 0.72, 40% of it unlit), outlines the \nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:2: * @file Outline shells (PLAN.md WP 7.2, §4.1, §6.7, Appendix B): the inverted hull, carried fro\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:3: * (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/00-setup.js:96-116`). A shell is the same mesh again, back faces\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:5: * width. `createOutline({ color, width, mode })` makes the material; `outline.shell(mesh)` adds\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:6: * its child, and `outline.batch(batch)` shells every page of an instanced batch (engine/gfx/ins\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:7: * shell sharing its instance matrices: call `sync()` after the batch's `end()`, and `register(w\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:9: * The push (`material.positionNode`, so the ID pass and every pass that copies it draw the shel\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:18: * advice `GFX_OUTLINE_UNPINNED` says so once, and instanced shells are pushed as if their inst","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d46f5b4-97b7-46a5-8fb8-5eac466a6eae","uuid":"b458a3f1-62af-4285-a010-e41f275b1feb","timestamp":"2026-11-05T11:09:43.066Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":" * outline.ts's inverted hulls, wired to the stage (engine/gfx/stage.ts) round its props and its bodies. Every batch\n * of the props (engine/gfx/props.ts, a shell per page sharing its instance matrices, pushed away from each part's\n * centre) and every actor's puppet (a skinned shell bound to its skeleton, pushed along its normals, so the line\n * follows the posed body, first person's hidden pieces hidden in it too) gets its shell as it first appears, at\n * `sync()`, which the stage runs at the end of each draw, so the instances and the pieces match the frame's.\n *\n * A look asks for them (`shells: { width, color }`, engine/gfx/post/looks.ts), which the page's look hands over each\n * frame (engine/app/look.ts): `width` in pixels at 270 lines, scaled in the shader to the picture's lines in whole\n * pixels, so the line keeps its weight in every resolution mode; 0 hides every shell. Showing, hiding, the width and\n * the colour are visibility and uniforms: the shells are registered with the warm-up whatever the look, so switching\n * builds nothing. The ID pass leaves them out (`userData.outline`, engine/gfx/idpass.ts): the shells are the look's,\n * not objects of their own, and a shot's objects are the same in every look.\n2: * @file The stage's outline shells (PLAN.md WP 13.24; docs/PLAYGROUND.md §5.2's cel look): engine/gfx/materials/\n9: * A look asks for them (`shells: { width, color }`, engine/gfx/post/looks.ts), which the page's look hands over each\n10: * frame (engine/app/look.ts): `width` in pixels at 270 lines, scaled in the shader to the picture's lines in whole\n11: * pixels, so the line keeps its weight in every resolution mode; 0 hides every shell. Showing, hiding, the width and\n12: * the colour are visibility and uniforms: the shells are registered with the warm-up whatever the look, so switching\n13: * builds nothing. The ID pass leaves them out (`userData.outline`, engine/gfx/idpass.ts): the shells are the look's,\n23: * // const shells = createStageShells({ props: stage.props, actors: stage.actors });\n24: * // shells.set({ width: 1, color: '#141018' }); // the cel look's\n25: * // stage.draw(alpha); shells.sync();\n30:import { shellsOn, type FeatureReport } from './features';\n38:/** The lines a look's shell width is given at: scaled to the picture's height in whole pixels. */\n41:/** What a look asks of the shells: their width in pixels at 270 lines (0 for none), and their colour, hex. */\n43:  width: number;\n47:/** The stage's shells (see the file comment). */\nengine/gfx/materials/toon.ts:7: * sun's light; a rim, gated by each light (a fresnel step at 0.72, 40% of it unlit), outlines the \nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:2: * @file Outline shells (PLAN.md WP 7.2, §4.1, §6.7, Appendix B): the inverted hull, carried fro\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:3: * (`my-3d2dge:src/stress-world/00-setup.js:96-116`). A shell is the same mesh again, back faces\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:5: * width. `createOutline({ color, width, mode })` makes the material; `outline.shell(mesh)` adds\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:6: * its child, and `outline.batch(batch)` shells every page of an instanced batch (engine/gfx/ins\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:7: * shell sharing its instance matrices: call `sync()` after the batch's `end()`, and `register(w\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:9: * The push (`material.positionNode`, so the ID pass and every pass that copies it draw the shel\nengine/gfx/materials/outline.ts:18: * advice `GFX_OUTLINE_UNPINNED` says so once, and instanced shells are pushed as if their inst","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HVymL4xd5mdWqgeYLxoXsR","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
