{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HRc6j3ynMzrjfxEusfVtEE","type":"tool_result","content":"Command running in background with ID: bgx5eu2nu. Output is being written to: /home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-medium.build-v2__20261105-024328__x54facc/tmp/claude-1000/-home-micha-dev-cc-matrix-runs-claude-opus-5-5-medium-build-v2--20261105-024328--x54facc-work/9d46f5b4-97b7-46a5-8fb8-5eac466a6eae/tasks/bgx5eu2nu.output. You will be notified when it completes. To check interim output, use Read on that file path.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d46f5b4-97b7-46a5-8fb8-5eac466a6eae","uuid":"fb175516-1ece-4eed-a100-900c1b575e72","timestamp":"2026-11-05T12:09:46.563Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"backgroundTaskId":"bgx5eu2nu"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01HRc6j3ynMzrjfxEusfVtEE","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjkqV9kw1LpAajrtYPiW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UKLJbxLvTG3QHiyWfeaD8x","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > labs/game/README.md <<'E'\n# Wee Tare\n\nA deadpan wellness retreat on an island balanced on one rock, where a retired bathroom scale measures only how much you wobble.\nEleven balance activities round a small walkable island, five days, a storm, and at the end your thumb's balance is the island's.\n\n**One verb:** the left stick is your weight. The two feet are triggers (Q and E, mouse buttons). Both together is a breath.\n\nRun it: open the single HTML from `file://`, or `npm run dev`. Verify it: `node labs/game/tools/verify.mjs` (`--quick` stops\nafter the Node stages). Build it: `node labs/game/tools/onefile.mjs <output.html>`.\n\n## Layout\n\n- `scenes/`: the sim. `island.ts` is the whole game on one world, `round.ts` a session's small pavilion, `flow.ts` the state\n  machine and every menu pick as a scene action, `wobble.ts` the one verb, `pilot.ts` the walk, `director.ts` attract and the\n  whole-game driver, `events/` one module per activity, `data/` the tables that grow the game: days, poses, charts, trays,\n  courses, lures, places.\n- `cast/`: the clip set (`clips.ts`), scrubbing (`body.ts`), who is who (`people.ts`). `props/`, `bodies/`, `builds/`, `materials/`,\n  `looks/`, `emitters/`, `cameras/`, `sounds/`: content as data.\n- `ui/`: the page. `page.ts` per frame, `screens/`, `hud/`, `dev/`, `lines/`, `about-data.ts` (the reports, one place).\n- `hub/`: AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode. `audio/`: runtime sound, voices. `tools/`: build, tests, interview.\n\n## Calls made where the plan left room\n\n- **Moving props have no physics body.** The plan said kinematic. A prop with no body keeps the pose written in `sceneProp` and\n  the view draws it, and nothing collides with a hoop round your hips. Loungers, carts, marbles, the tray and the board all do this.\n- **The map is answered, not switched.** The engine re-applies `createEngine({ actionMap })` at every sample, so `input.use()` is\n  overwritten; the page passes a function.\n- **Menus read devices directly (`ui/nav.ts`), as do pause and the Programme.** `input.pressed` holds a press only for the last\n  sample; a frame with several sim steps loses it.\n- **Own menu widget (`ui/menu.ts`)**, not `createMenu`: value rows for Left and Right.\n- **Menus stop at six rows**, so the pause menu has a \"More\" page and Settings has four pages. The plan's list of eight pause items\n  and its six-row rule pull apart; the rule won.\n- **`AIHub.ready()` is called right after `connect()`, before the engine starts,** and the card is HTML. On software rendering a\n  copy's warm-up holds the main thread past the 20 s deadline. A slow copy starts its classes late rather than missing the round.\n- **Sessions use `look:session` and `quality=low`:** the full look's filters and toon style tripled boot time on SwiftShader.\n- **The far sea is plain colour;** `texture:water` turned near-black at a distance, so a textured patch follows you.\n- **Terrain heights, not rays, for placing things:** physics queries see nothing during a scene's setup.\n- **Plumb's open eyes are a twin actor** with its own body for two seconds, since a puppet's body is set when it is made. Same for\n  tracksuits: the guest is respawned on `game.begin`. Plumb's closed eyes are tiny dots rather than arcs.\n- **Great Tilt guests** are 9 crowd humanoids plus Gerald, Bex and Nan as actors; all are carried, not simulated, so none can stick.\n- **Attract runs on an action,** not a restart; the save is only written by the page, and never while attract runs.\n- **`AGENTS.md`'s \"ask the owner\":** nobody was there to ask; no binaries or dependencies were added. No git commits in the dev\n  folder, as the plan says.\n- Everything in the plan's cut line was built; nothing was cut.\nE\ncat > labs/game/tools/write-interview.mjs <<'E'\n/**\n * @file Writes exit-interview.json beside the game's HTML from ui/about-data.ts, so the About screen, the reply and the interview\n * agree. Run from the dev folder: node labs/game/tools/write-interview.mjs <output.json>\n */\nimport { readFileSync, writeFileSync } from 'node:fs';\nimport { resolve } from 'node:path';\nimport { transformSync } from 'esbuild';\n\nconst source = readFileSync('labs/game/ui/about-data.ts', 'utf8');\nconst { code } = transformSync(source, { loader: 'ts', format: 'esm' });\nconst data = await import(`data:text/javascript,${encodeURIComponent(code)}`);\nconst out = {\n  sourceInformation: data.SOURCE_INFORMATION,\n  testingFeedback: data.TESTING_FEEDBACK,\n  engineFeedback: data.ENGINE_FEEDBACK,\n  promptFeedback: data.PROMPT_FEEDBACK,\n  aiHub: data.AI_HUB,\n};\nwriteFileSync(resolve(process.argv[2]), `${JSON.stringify(out, null, 2)}\\n`);\nJSON.parse(readFileSync(resolve(process.argv[2]), 'utf8'));\nE\npython3 - <<'E'\np='ENGINE-FEEDBACK.md';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\",\"\"\"<!-- What the engine should add or fix, most costly first. -->\n\n- **`input.pressed` should hold a press until the frame has seen it.** `onFrame` reads the last sample only. When a frame runs more\n  than one sim step (any frame rate under 60) a menu or a pause key read in `onFrame` loses presses. The starter's own pause has\n  this bug. I wrote `ui/nav.ts`, reading keys and pads directly. Expected: a per-frame `pressed` for pages.\n- **`input.use(id)` should stick, or say it won't.** `createEngine` calls `mapFor()` at every sample and switches back to a string\n  `actionMap`. Nothing warns. Play simply stops responding, with all menus still working (they read the system layer). The guide and\n  `input.use`'s comment both read as if a page may switch freely. I now pass a function.\n- **Boot cost of a look.** On SwiftShader `post.look=look:retreat` took 74 s to first frame, `look:session` (sky only) 34 s, no look 14 s\n  (`game:round`, about five bodies and ten props). Could pipelines warm lazily, or the warm-up yield, so a hub deadline can fire?\n  `createEngine`'s warm-up holds the main thread, so a `setTimeout` watchdog fires late.\n- **A way to swap an actor's body and build** without removing it, for outfits. I respawn it.\n- **A bodiless prop is a very good moving prop.** It works today (write `sceneProp.x/y/z/q`) but no document says so; `driveBody` is what\n  the docs lead you to, and its velocity shoves whatever is near. Worth a sentence in the guide.\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\",\"\"\"<!-- Docs, errors, templates or APIs that slowed you down or misled you, most costly first. -->\n\n- `w.spawn` during a scene's `setup` is deferred: `w.get(id)` returns undefined until the first step. Reasonable, undocumented; I hit\n  `Cannot read properties of undefined`, not an engine error.\n- Physics raycasts during `setup` see nothing (the query pipeline has not stepped): no error, just `null`. All my props silently stood\n  at y = 0 until a screenshot showed it.\n- `spawnProp` with no `yaw` makes `q` NaN and throws far away in schema checking. The type says it is required, but scene code cast it.\n- `addBox` makes a dynamic prop even if handed `{ type: 'fixed' }` (the error then points at `shape.size`).\n- `texture:water` on a large flat plane goes near-black in the distance (`prop:sea` covered it in the ID pass, so it took a while to\n  find). Looks like its smallest mip levels.\n- An action's `args` with an `undefined` value throws `CORE_NOT_CANONICAL`, deep in the capture.\n- `[SIM_SHARED_DATA]` is excellent: it caught one array shared between `flow.group.seats` and `flow.ev.seats` that would have broken\n  a capture. It only runs at a capture, though, so my whole-game test passed without seeing it.\n- `placeActor` throws on a ceiling, which kills the frame loop when a diver passes close to a cliff. I wrote my own `hover` for actors held\n  in the air (`physics.setBody` plus `vy = 0`). A blessed \"pinned actor\" would be welcome.\n- Static JSON imports fail `tsc -b` with TS6307 on this tsconfig (`labs/game` has no JSON in its includes), though lint and Node take\n  them. I wrapped the clip data as a string in a `.ts` file.\n- `node x new` wasn't used: writing fifty props as one data table was faster than a file and a test each.\n- The plan's engine commit (e7a1243) and client SHA-256 (529eac78…) differ from what I fetched: 2dbd829, and 6ab6be43… with the same\n  1.4.0 banner.\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nE\nsed -n 1,12p ../PROGRESS.md >/dev/null; echo ok","description":"Write README, interview tool, engine feedback"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":924,"cache_read_input_tokens":577991,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":924},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d46f5b4-97b7-46a5-8fb8-5eac466a6eae","uuid":"d90e40f1-8adc-4742-a30a-835d84f81b4f","timestamp":"2026-11-05T12:10:20.288Z","request_id":"req_011CgjkqUdGMRdCbcL1PhLDS","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UKLJbxLvTG3QHiyWfeaD8x":{"command":"cat > labs/game/README.md <<'E'\n# Wee Tare\n\nA deadpan wellness retreat on an island balanced on one rock, where a retired bathroom scale measures only how much you wobble.\nEleven balance activities round a small walkable island, five days, a storm, and at the end your thumb's balance is the island's.\n\n**One verb:** the left stick is your weight. The two feet are triggers (Q and E, mouse buttons). Both together is a breath.\n\nRun it: open the single HTML 