{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgjnS9iZJhdWUBEms3rdJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XNYm1RDxFLrSGTBHFeL6ri","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\nimport re\np='labs/game/ui/about-data.ts';s=open(p).read()\nblocks={\n\"TESTING_FEEDBACK\":\"\"\"export const TESTING_FEEDBACK: readonly string[] = [\n  'About 25 real issues, not counting typos the compiler or a first boot caught: bots stepping every frame, the Line finishing in 7 seconds, group state leaking into the finale, a shared array only a capture would notice, props at height zero, the map being switched back, lost presses, Esc closing its own pause, a pad press that left attract and also picked Begin, and more.',\n  'About 6: play ignoring all input after the first map switch; Esc never pausing; the session scene failing its boot deadline; the finale never ending in the whole-game run; a diver crashing the frame loop against the cliff; every prop standing at height zero.',\n  'The browser script that plays through the built file with real keys and a stubbed pad. It found the worst bugs, all of which every Node test had passed. The whole-game bot run was next: it found the stall on Day 5.',\n  'The first hub harness run at 8 seconds of play: it passed while the engine had not finished starting in either frame, so it proved the protocol and nothing about the game. It needed a longer run with the engine checked in each frame.',\n];\"\"\",\n\"ENGINE_FEEDBACK\":\"\"\"export const ENGINE_FEEDBACK: readonly string[] = [\n  'Scrubbing poses as plain data. A readable clip set, with slots I can write each step, made a body that follows your thumb in a few lines, and the same code runs in Node with a stable hash. Headless play made a full bot playthrough cheap.',\n  'Yes. I assumed input.use switches maps for good, but a string actionMap is re-applied at every sample. I assumed input.pressed read in onFrame sees every press, and it does not above one sim step per frame. I also guessed geometry parameters and the shape of vib wrongly, and those errors were clear.',\n  'The Wobble Model and the bots that stand in for a human, then the 10-foot menu layer and the camera shot table.',\n  'Startup and placement order: spawns and physics queries are not ready during setup, placeActor throws where a diver passes a cliff, and a look costs tens of seconds of warm-up on software rendering, holding the main thread past the hub deadline.',\n  'None. The engine is unchanged.',\n  'A per-frame input.pressed that never loses a press, and an action map that stays where a page puts it.',\n];\"\"\",\n\"PROMPT_FEEDBACK\":\"\"\"export const PROMPT_FEEDBACK: readonly string[] = [\n  'The tested marks in the plan. Knowing which numbers had really been run (the sway rate above all) saved hours, and the writing samples set the tone at once.',\n  'Pause lists eight items while the 10-foot rule allows six rows, and the client SHA-256 and engine commit in the plan differed from what I fetched. It says to compare, so that was survivable. Moving props on kinematic bodies was stated firmly though a bodiless prop is simpler.',\n  'Judging feel with nobody to play: every balance number rests on a model of a thumb. Also proving things on a shared software renderer, where frames take seconds and memory runs out.',\n  'I would ask for browser play tests early rather than late in the build order, say what real frame rate to assume on this machine, and let the look of a session be simple from the start.',\n];\"\"\",\n}\nfor k,v in blocks.items():\n    s=re.sub(r\"export const \"+k+r\": readonly string\\[\\] = \\[.*?\\];\",lambda m:v,s,count=1,flags=re.S)\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='labs/game/tools/browser.py';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"check('a slider changes the setting', pg.evaluate(\"(p)=>__game.setting(p)\", PATH) == 7,\"\"\",\"\"\"check('a slider changes the setting', abs(pg.evaluate(\"(p)=>__game.setting(p)\", PATH) - 7) < 0.1,\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"    pg.mouse.move(1200, 300, steps=4)\n    time.sleep(0.4)\"\"\",\"\"\"    pg.evaluate(\"()=>{for(let k=0;k<5;k++)window.dispatchEvent(new PointerEvent('pointermove',{movementX:60,movementY:0,bubbles:true,pointerType:'mouse'}))}\")\n    time.sleep(0.6)\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"check('no touch controls', pg.evaluate(\"()=>document.querySelectorAll('[data-ui^=touch],.touch-stick,.touch-button,.touch-fan').length===0\"))\"\"\",\"\"\"touchy = \"()=>[...document.querySelectorAll('[data-ui^=touch],[class*=touch i],[id*=touch i]')].filter(e=>getComputedStyle(e).display!=='none').map(e=>e.tagName+'.'+e.className+'#'+e.id)\"\n    check('no touch controls', not pg.evaluate(touchy), pg.evaluate(touchy))\"\"\")\ns=s.replace(\"\"\"check('Reset restores the default', pg.evaluate(\"(p)=>__game.setting(p)\", PATH) == 3.5,\"\"\",\"\"\"check('Reset restores the default', abs(pg.evaluate(\"(p)=>__game.setting(p)\", PATH) - 3.5) < 1e-6,\"\"\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\np='labs/game/ui/dev/panel.ts';s=open(p).read()\ns=s.replace(\"const start = Math.max(0, Math.min(rows.length - VISIBLE, at - 6));\",\"if (!hovering) top = Math.max(0, Math.min(rows.length - VISIBLE, at < top ? at : at >= top + VISIBLE ? at - VISIBLE + 1 : top));\\n    hovering = false;\\n    const start = top;\")\ns=s.replace(\"  const VISIBLE = 13;\",\"  const VISIBLE = 13;\\n  let top = 0;\\n  let hovering = false;\")\ns=s.replace(\"if (event.pointerType === 'mouse' && at !== i) { at = i; paintFocus(); }\",\"if (event.pointerType === 'mouse' && at !== i) { at = i; hovering = true; paintFocus(); }\")\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nprint('hovering = true' in s)\nE\ngrep -n \"game.day\\|Jump to Day\\|nth=2\" labs/game/tools/browser.py | head -4 | cut -c1-90; npx prettier --write labs/game/ui --log-level warn; npx tsc -b tsconfig.check.json 2>&1 | head -5 | cut -c1-170; out/t/b.sh; timeout 590 python3 -u labs/game/tools/browser.py \"$PWD/../WeeTare-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105