{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01S9fXrLG7YP6QfjkYuB8vjW","type":"tool_result","content":"Build the game PLAN.md describes. Take your file names and what to hand in from TASK.md, which is filled in for you. Keep your progress in PROGRESS.md, so you can pick up where you were after your context is compacted.\n17:    \"test\": \"vitest run\"\nengine/dev/actions.ts:8: *   with what it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action) or `settings` alone (recorded as set, view ones never).\nengine/dev/actions.ts:13: *   step is recorded (`input.record()` replays it). With `seeds` (`1-20`, `5`, `3,7,9`), a sweep from fresh sessions\nengine/dev/actions.ts:14: *   of the scene with this run's recorded settings instead, the run itself left alone: one row, a run per seed.\nengine/dev/actions.ts:16: * Invariants: members change the sim only through the session's recorded operations (engine/dev/members.ts); this\nengine/dev/actions.ts:41:  /** What it changes: `sim` (recorded as a dev action), or `settings` alone (recorded as set, but view ones). */\nengine/dev/actions.ts:69:  help: \"Runs a dev action between steps, recorded in the replay: actions.run('travel', { at: [3, 0, 5] }).\",\nengine/dev/galleryScene.ts:15: * The recorded settings `gallery.kind`, `gallery.subject` and `gallery.state` stage the first entry (a deep link,\nengine/dev/overlay.ts:6: * `error(record)` shows `CODE: message` and `Fix: …` and keeps the first error on screen (a later one is counted,\nengine/dev/overlay.ts:9: * Invariants: DOM only, no engine state: the records it shows are the log's (`__engine.errors`), so the overlay and\nengine/dev/overlay.ts:31:  error(record: OverlayRecord): void;\nengine/dev/overlay.ts:68:    error(record) {\nengine/dev/overlay.ts:70:      else first = { code: record.code, message: record.message, fix: record.fix };\nx help: ok: node x replay <file|dir…> [--update] [--browser sim|page] [--bisect] [--runs n] [--swap names] [--state] [--until n]\nReplays against their golden hashes (PLAN.md §8.4, §6.5 items 8–9, WPs 1.5 and 2.7). Usage: node x replay\n<file|dir…> [--update] [--browser sim|page] [--bisect] [--runs n] [--swap names] [--state] [--until n]. Exit 0 when\nevery replay gives its goldens in every run (or, recorded elsewhere, agrees with itself; or was recorded), 1\notherwise, 2 on a usage error. The verdict never says \"match\" unless this platform's goldens were compared.\n\n`--state` writes the state a replay ends in, as Node plays it: its canonical state and event trace, as `x sim`\nwrites its own, to `out/replay/<name>/state.json` (`<name>`: the file's, without `.replay.json`); `--until n` (it\nimplies `--state`) writes the state after step n instead. So an agent reads where a run left its bodies, its props\nand its components without a page or a probe of its own (tools/lib/replayState.ts).\n\nEach `*.replay.json` (a directory means every one under it) plays from step 0 in Node, `--runs` times (3), and with\n`--browser sim` as often again in Chromium, in tests/pages/replay.html: the sim in a page, no renderer, through the\nsame player (engine/sim/replay.ts). Every run must give the goldens of this platform (`linux-x64`): one set, valid\nin Node and in Chromium alike (`judgeRuns`). A replay recorded on another platform only runs at least twice and\ncompares the runs (\"golden: other platform\"). Its scene module is found from its `scene` id, as `x sim` finds it,\nand loads after the animation library, as there (tools/anim/library.ts; the page: tests/pages/replay.ts).\n`--browser page` plays each replay in its scene's own page instead (`labs/<name>/?scene=<scene>` for a module under\n… 17 more in out/help/replay/output.txt\nreport: out/help/replay/report.json\n55:    include: [\n78:    include: ['**/*.test.ts'],","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d46f5b4-97b7-46a5-8fb8-5eac466a6eae","uuid":"f721cc53-79f0-4804-bef4-9ff53fd274c4","timestamp":"2026-11-05T14:40:38.035Z"