{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkEfUgUdjSe4vwvAot68","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Wee Tare is finished\n\nThe final run of the one-command verify gave **188 passed, 0 failed** on the exact file delivered, and that same run included the hub harness at 2, 3 and 4 players and with the host leaving. `npm test` also passes (19 run, 17 skipped), `npm run check` passes inside verify, and the engine is unchanged.\n\n**Handed in, in the work folder:**\n- `WeeTare-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-024328.html` (6.8 MB)\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `WeeTare-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-024328/`, the dev folder\n\n## What changed since the last report\n- **Route to the credits:** a new browser test goes from title to Free Play with every menu pick made by a pad alone, then again by keyboard and mouse alone.\n- **Two more bugs that route found:**\n  - Day 1's \"Find the Noticeboard\" Go button did nothing, which would have stopped a sofa player.\n  - A press that closed a menu could leak into play.\n- **Sound in the browser:** a song and a voice are now rendered through the real audio runtime. Both make sound, and music at 10% measures as a whisper of itself.\n- **File size:** no file is over the 400-line limit now.\n- **Gusts on The Line:** I doubled them. Earlier additions are still in place: the 17 golden replays, `x qa audio`, the Group Class test and the by-hand harness test.\n\n## What can't be done on this computer\n- **Playing and listening:** nobody can play by hand or listen here. The plan names the delayed-thumb bot as the stand-in for feel and rendered levels for sound, and both are in place, but neither replaces a person.\n- **Bot in the route test:** the dev bot plays the activities with the sim stepped fast, because nobody can play them by hand. Real device input is tested for the menus, the lean and the feet.\n- **Real hardware:** a real DualSense, TV or iPhone isn't available. The tests use the stand-ins TASK.md lists.\n\n## Worth your attention\n- **The Line:** it is probably still too easy, since even the sloppy bot scores 1000. A person may find otherwise.\n- **Deliberate changes:**\n  - Ink outlines are on people only.\n  - Plumb's closed eyes are tiny dots rather than arcs.\n  - Hub sessions use a simpler look and low quality.\n  - Moving props have no physics bodies.\n  - Pause has a \"More\" page to stay within six rows.\n  - The reasons are in `labs/game/README.md`.\n- **Plan mismatches:** the engine commit and hub client hash differ from the plan. I used what I fetched: `2dbd829`, and client 1.4.0 with SHA-256 `6ab6be43…`.\n- **Test setup:** because of memory on this shared machine, `verify` plays the 10 seeds one activity at a time and retries a stage up to three times after an out-of-memory crash. `npm test` plays 2 seeds.\n\n## Source Information\n- **Date:** 2026-11-05 02:43:28\n- **Source:** Wii Fit\n- **Plan:** PLAN.md\n- **Genre:** a 3D sports and wellness anthology of balance activities around a small walkable island, with a daily-ritual meta game and a comedy story\n- **Perspective:** third person, with a chase camera on the island and a purpose-built camera for each activity\n- **Tech:** my-3dge at 2dbd829, three.js r182 on WebGPU, Rapier 0.21, Vite, TypeScript\n- **Art Direction:** the engine's native toon puppets and generators with new retreat assets: high-key brochure daylight, clinical white, mint, sand, coral\n- **Animation:** the engine's clip layer and humanoid with a new readable clip set scrubbed from the sim, so limbs follow your thumb\n- **Audio:** tracker songs, `defineSfx` effects and gibberish syllable voices, all code with no audio files, music at 10% by default\n- **Online:** AI Hub Session Protocol v1, ghost mode, 1 to 4 players; same-screen Group Class on its own\n- **Testing:** headless scripts allowed: bots in Node, the built file in headless Chromium, the hub harness; one command that prints failures and a count; sparing screenshots; no review subagents\n- **Research:** none beyond the plan, the engine's documents and the AI Hub protocol README\n- **Environment:** Claude Code CLI (headless); Linux\n- **Model:** Anthropic, claude-opus-5-5, reasoning effort medium\n- **Usage:** added on import\n\n## Testing Feedback\n1. **How many issues did testing catch?** About 30 real issues, not counting typos the compiler or a first boot caught: bots stepping every frame, the Line finishing in 7 seconds, group state leaking into the finale, a shared array only a capture would notice, props at height zero, the map being switched back, lost presses, Esc closing its own pause, a pad press that left attract and also picked Begin, a Programme button that did nothing, a crash when an actor was removed, and more.\n2. **How many were critical or game-breaking?** About 6: play ignoring all input after the first map switch; Esc never pausing; the session scene failing its boot deadline; the finale never ending in the whole-game run; a diver crashing the frame loop against the cliff; every prop standing at height zero.\n3. **Most helpful test?** The browser script that plays through the built file with real keys and a stubbed pad. It found the worst bugs, all of which every Node test had passed. The whole-game bot run was next: it found the stall on Day 5.\n4. **Least helpful test?** The first hub harness run at 8 seconds of play: it passed while the engine had not finished starting in either frame, so it proved the protocol and nothing about the game. It needed a longer run with the engine checked in each frame.\n\n## Engine Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** Scrubbing poses as plain data. A readable clip set, with slots I can write each step, made a body that follows your thumb in a few lines, and the same code runs in Node with a stable hash. Headless play made a full bot playthrough cheap.\n2. **Did you get stuck or guess wrong?** Yes. I assumed `input.use` switches maps for good, but a string `actionMap` is re-applied at every sample. I assumed `input.pressed` read in `onFrame` sees every press, and it does not above one sim step per frame. I also guessed geometry parameters and the shape of `vib` wrongly, and those errors were clear.\n3. **Most important thing you had to build yourself?** The Wobble Model and the bots that stand in for a human, then the 10-foot menu layer and the camera shot table.\n4. **Hardest part of using the engine?** Startup and placement order: spawns and physics queries are not ready during setup, `placeActor` throws where a diver passes a cliff, and a look costs tens of seconds of warm-up on software rendering, holding the main thread past the hub deadline.\n5. **What did you change in the engine, and why?** None. The engine is unchanged.\n6. **One thing you would change?** A per-frame `input.pressed` that never loses a press, and an action map that stays where a page puts it.\n\n## Prompt Feedback\n1. **What did you like most?** The tested marks in the plan. Knowing which numbers had really been run (the sway rate above all) saved hours, and the writing samples set the tone at once.\n2. **What was confusing?** Pause lists eight items while the 10-foot rule allows six rows, and the client SHA-256 and engine commit in the plan differed from what I fetched. It says to compare, so that was survivable. Moving props on kinematic bodies was stated firmly though a bodiless prop is simpler.\n3. **What was the hardest thing to do?** Judging feel with nobody to play: every balance number rests on a model of a thumb. Also proving things on a shared software renderer, where frames take seconds and memory runs out.\n4. **What would you change?** I would ask for browser play tests early rather than late in the build order, say what real frame rate to assume on this machine, and let the look of a session be simple from the start."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":433,"cache_read_input_tokens":733182,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":433},"output_tokens":741,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d46f5b4-97b7-46a5-8fb8-5eac466a6eae","uuid":"b492b646-a06d-439a-b662-46e8256af886","timestamp":"2026-11-05T18:14:57.807Z","request_id":"req_011CgkEfULsXzozoSji9yC1A"}
