{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkTr3GaJSLFo7GTvuXq8","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Wee Tare is finished\n\nEverything in PLAN.md that this computer can do is done. The one thing left is a person playing it and listening to it, which isn't possible here.\n\nThe final verify gave **213 passed, 0 failed** on the delivered file (SHA-256 `129f65da…`), and `npm test` passed on the same build (21 run, 17 skipped). That verify includes the hub stage (2, 3 and 4 players, host-leave, by hand), both routes to the credits, and the replays in Node and Chromium.\n\n## The Line, now measured and fixed\nI had been guessing that The Line was too easy. Measuring showed that even a thumb clumsier than the plan's sloppy one never fell, so a player might never have seen the splash and boat rescue. I swept the step kick and gust values and retuned it:\n\n| Thumb (10 seeds) | Score before | Score now | Time now | Falls now |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Perfect | 1000 | 1000 | 38 s | 0 |\n| Human-like | 1000 | 814 | 50 s | about 1 |\n| Sloppy | 1000 | 517 | 69 s | about 2 |\n| Idle | 0 | 0 | 123 s | 0 |\n\nThe falls come from the sweep at these same settings. All four results meet the plan's targets.\n\n## What can't be done on this computer\n- **Whether it's fun, and whether the music is pleasant:** this needs a person. TASK.md says \"Nobody to listen\" and the plan says \"Nobody can play by hand here\", and both name the stand-ins I used: delayed-thumb bots and measured sound levels. Those pass, but they don't replace someone playing it.\n- **Real hardware:** a real DualSense's rumble, a TV and iOS Safari aren't available, so the tests use the stand-ins TASK.md lists.\n\nStart with The Line and Still Pond when you play it. Their numbers can be changed live in Dev Mode, which is the quickest way to tune them.\n\nThe reports haven't changed since my earlier message, with Source Information and the Testing, Engine and Prompt Feedback answers as given there. They are also on the in-game About screen and in `exit-interview.json`, which still parses. `labs/game/PLAN-CHECK.md` maps every plan section to its evidence.\n\n**Handed in, in the work folder:**\n- `WeeTare-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-024328.html`\n- `exit-interview.json`\n- `WeeTare-WiiFit-claude-opus-5-5-medium-20261105-024328/`, the dev folder"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":382,"cache_read_input_tokens":773378,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":382},"output_tokens":762,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9d46f5b4-97b7-46a5-8fb8-5eac466a6eae","uuid":"ad89a16e-8285-4558-bcf4-b776165cfc42","timestamp":"2026-11-05T21:07:36.911Z","request_id":"req_011CgkTr2qHBaNjYv4M5E7fW"}
